 \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace tests/daemon-api-error-handling.test.ts (148 lines) and tests/daemon-api-projects.test.ts (235 lines) with Playwright E2E tests. Both are all static analysis.\\n\\nWrite: packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-errors.spec.ts (or extend existing errors.spec.ts which currently uses mocks)\\nUsing: daemon fixture from tests/fixtures/test-base.ts\\n\\nError handling — make real requests that trigger each error type:\\n- GET /api/tasks/nonexistent-ref — 404 with {error, message, suggestion} (@api-contract ac-22)\\n- POST /api/tasks/:ref/note with empty body — 400 with {error, details:[{field, message}]} (@api-contract ac-23)\\n- POST /api/tasks/:ref/start on already-started task — 409 with {error, current, valid_transitions} (@api-contract ac-24)\\n\\nNote: existing errors.spec.ts uses route.fulfill() mocks. The new tests should hit the REAL daemon instead. Either extend that file with a real-daemon section or create api-errors.spec.ts.\\n\\nProjects API (uses daemon.createSecondProject helper):\\n- GET /api/projects — list registered projects with paths and watcherStatus (@multi-directory-daemon ac-28)\\n- POST /api/projects — register project with path validation (@multi-directory-daemon ac-29)\\n- DELETE /api/projects/:encodedPath — unregister project (@multi-directory-daemon ac-30)\\n\\nAfter E2E tests pass, delete both static files.\\nRun: npm test && npm run test:e2e to verify.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #551. Replaced tests/daemon-api-error-handling.test.ts (148 lines) and tests/daemon-api-projects.test.ts (235 lines) with Playwright E2E tests. Created packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-errors.spec.ts (33 tests) covering @api-contract ac-22, ac-23, ac-24 with real HTTP calls to running daemon. Created packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-projects.spec.ts (13 tests) covering @multi-directory-daemon ac-28, ac-29, ac-30. Fix cycle resolved: corrected ac-23 to use custom 400 handler validation (whitespace text), fixed ac-5/6/7 misannotations to use ac-29, added explicit POST response assertion test. Resolved 3 unresolved GitHub review threads. All CI checks passing.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"daemon\",\n      \"e2e\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJCTE1GG3AZEHZ5YWTTHWCHF\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:28:49.241Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:45:27.209Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:45:30.587Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:45:57.259Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJCTPC9QPYRQ5ESZXJVTCQV7\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:17:39.255Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Reading existing test files: daemon-api-error-handling.test.ts (148 lines, static analysis) and daemon-api-projects.test.ts (235 lines, static/documentary tests). Projects route is fully implemented in packages/daemon/src/routes/projects.ts. Writing api-errors.spec.ts for error handling ACs (ac-22, ac-23, ac-24) and api-projects.spec.ts for projects API ACs (ac-28, ac-29, ac-30). Existing errors.spec.ts uses mocks — creating separate api-errors.spec.ts for real daemon tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJCV8F93ECZTVF1GMCTDCX6A\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:27:32.131Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Created packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-errors.spec.ts (33 tests) covering @api-contract ac-22, ac-23, ac-24 with real HTTP calls. Created packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-projects.spec.ts (13 tests) covering @multi-directory-daemon ac-28, ac-29, ac-30. Deleted tests/daemon-api-error-handling.test.ts (148 lines) and tests/daemon-api-projects.test.ts (235 lines). All unit test suites pass (54 files,