 GET request or WebSocket event) (@daemon-server ac-4)\\n- Verify debounce: rapid successive file changes result in a single reparse (@daemon-server ac-5)\\n- Verify YAML parse errors don't crash the watcher — modify file to invalid YAML, then fix it (@daemon-server ac-6)\\n\\nNote: CI (GitHub Actions) does not support recursive fs.watch — file watcher tests are skipped in CI. Add the same skip condition used by other watcher tests. Check the convention in kspec-agents.md: 'File watcher tests skip in CI'.\\n\\nAfter E2E tests pass, delete tests/daemon-watcher.test.ts.\\nRun: npm test && npm run test:e2e to verify.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #557. Replaced tests/daemon-watcher.test.ts (163 lines of static analysis) with packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-watcher.spec.ts (582 lines of behavioral E2E tests). 6 tests covering @daemon-server ac-4 (file change detection + API mutation), ac-5 (debounce verification, 2 tests), ac-6 (YAML error broadcast + recovery). Fixed Codex review race conditions by adding installBroadcastCounter() two-phase pattern. Added N/A annotations for ac-7/ac-8 (not testable in E2E). All CI checks passed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"daemon\",\n      \"e2e\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJD384ABVWV1CVHJX0B5PJYA\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:28:56.244Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:47:45.592Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:01:38.950Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:22:54.362Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJD41Y7CED4AX4MYQC7XAGAJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:01:15.244Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Created packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-watcher.spec.ts with 6 E2E tests covering @daemon-server ac-4, ac-5, ac-6. Tests use page.evaluate() with native browser WebSocket API to subscribe to files:updates and files:errors topics, then write YAML files directly to daemon.kspecDir from Node.js context to trigger the watcher. All trait ACs annotated N/A with reasons. CI skip added via testInfo.skip(process.env.CI) — file watcher tests skip in CI as per convention. Deleted daemon-watcher.test.ts (163 lines of static analysis). All 3524 unit tests pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBNJKVJWSX2240N81H9KYYA\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-delete-static-analysis-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Delete static analysis tests for ralph end-loop, web-ui-triage, and misc\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Delete static analysis tests that have behavioral coverage elsewhere or test things that don't need testing. Where gaps exist, add behavioral replacements.\\n\\nFiles to DELETE entirely:\\n1. tests/skill-module-split.test.ts (121 lines) — tests that a code split happened. The split is done. Re-exports are proven by actual usage.\\n2. tests/web-ui-shared-types.test.ts (61 lines) — convention enforcement guard for 2 files, not behavior.\\n3. tests/web-ui-triage.test.ts (300 lines) — reads Svelte components for string patterns. UI behavior covered by E2E.\\n\\nPartial deletes in tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts:\\n- DELETE lines 254-272 (ac-detect): covered by behavioral tests at lines 148-251.\\n- DELETE lines 348-372 (ac-remove-markers): absence tests checking removed marker code stays removed. Not behavior — nobody is reintroducing deleted marker file code.\\n- DELETE lines 374-418 (trait error-guidance): exact duplicates of lines 120-144.\\n- DELETE lines 493-502 (closeSession export check): string matching on store.ts source.\\n- REPLACE lines 277-346 (session close handlers) with behavioral tests: the static tests check for signal handler registration and close_reason strings in ralph.ts source. session-budget-integration.test.ts lines 420-548 already verify status (completed/abandoned) and signal names, but do NOT verify close_reason text. Add behavioral assertions to the existing spawnRalphUntil tests that read session.yaml and check close_reason contains the expected text (e.g. \\\"Completed all iterations\\\", \\\"Received SIGINT\\\", \\\"Received SIGTERM\\\"). Then delete lines 277-346. Annotate the new assertions with // AC: @session-end-loop-signal ac-session-close-normal, ac-session-close-signal, ac-session-close-error.\\n- KEEP: lines 1-252 (behavioral), 423-478 (behavioral CLI tests).\\n\\nPartial deletes in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts:\\n- DELETE lines 293-339 (ac-remove-marker-code): 13 absence tests checking 26 removed marker patterns in ralph.ts. Same rationale — nobody is reintroducing deleted marker file code.\\n- KEEP: lines 1-290 (behavioral budget tests), 341-548 (behavioral session close tests).\\n\\nOther partial deletes:\\n5. tests/normalize-ref-input.test.ts — delete lines 37-139 (anti-pattern scanning and import checks). Keep lines 1-35 (unit tests for normalizeRefInput function).\\n6. tests/package-distribution.test.ts — delete lines 20-46 (directory existence via fs.stat) and lines 57-62 (directory count). Keep lines 50-55, 64-91, 94-185 (content validation, npm packaging, plugin integrity).\\n\\nRun: npm test to verify no regressions.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #558. Deleted 869 lines of static analysis tests across 7 files. Added behavioral replacements: close_reason assertions for session close paths, new ac-session-close-error test using --max-failures 1, N/A annotations for ac-detect and ac-remove-markers. All Codex review findings addressed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJD384ABVWV1CVHJX0B5PJYA\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:28:58.610Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:58:10.500Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:58:16.191Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:58:17.442Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJD5W4KAJZCFD2SSSXN6K0H0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:33:02.315Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Deleted 3 test files entirely (skill-module-split.test.ts, web-ui-shared-types.test.ts, web-ui-triage.test.ts). Made partial deletes in 4 more files: end-loop.test.ts (removed ac-detect static, session close handlers static, ac-remove-markers, trait error-guidance duplicates, closeSession export check), session-budget-integration.test.ts (removed ac-remove-marker-code block + added behavioral close_reason assertions to spawnRalphUntil tests), normalize-ref-input.test.ts (removed static analysis and import checks), package-distribution.test.ts (removed directory existence fs.stat tests and directory count test). Added AC annotations for ac-session-close-normal/signal/error to behavioral tests. All 3431 tests pass across all 3 shards.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJD60DRN2WXRX8QPB5MRC373\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:35:22.773Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"PR #558 created. Deleted 869 lines of static analysis tests across 7 files. Replaced with behavioral close_reason assertions in session-budget-integration.test.ts. Fixed test assertion for crash agent path (close_reason is 'Completed all 1 iterations' not 'abandoned' when using --max-loops 1). All shards pass locally.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJD6F0DEP9QYHT60DDHK1K4Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:43:20.623Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Codex review found 2 MUST-FIX coverage regressions: (1) @interactive-triage-ui ac-1 through ac-8 had no coverage after deleting web-ui-triage.test.ts — fixed by creating packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/triage.spec.ts with 9 behavioral E2E tests testing the real triage UI page; (2) @package-distribution ac-1 and ac-2 had no annotations after removing the fs.stat directory tests — fixed by adding AC annotations to the manifest.yaml content test, hooks/ file test, and agents-sections/ readdir test. Also updated stale N/A references in api-triage.spec.ts pointing to deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts. All fixes pushed to PR #558.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJD6RPEY79MXYKRN10SBHVDG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:48:38.110Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: 2 MUST-FIX items found in PR review: (1) @interactive-triage-ui ac-6 has no // AC: annotation in triage.spec.ts — header claims coverage but no per-test annotation exists; needs either a behavioral E2E test for WebSocket real-time updates or a file-level N/A annotation with reason. (2) check-unresolved-comments CI failing because the first chapel review thread (ac-session-close-error) is unresolved even though outdated — resolve it to unblock CI. All other items pass: new ac-session-close-error test using --max-failures 1 is correct behavioral coverage, N/A annotations formatted properly, package-distribution per-test annotations added. Review posted at https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/558#issuecomment-3967105194\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJBNZKQA8XAVYF9NQVQRXNRQ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-lint-no-static-analysis-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add CI lint to prevent static analysis test pattern\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add a vitest test that fails if any test file reads source code files — the static analysis anti-pattern this project is migrating away from.\\n\\nThe pattern to detect: test files under tests/ that use readFile/readFileSync on paths containing src/ or packages/*/src/. These read implementation source code and assert on string patterns instead of testing behavior.\\n\\nApproach: Write tests/lint/no-static-analysis.test.ts that:\\n1. Globs all tests/**/*.test.ts files\\n2. Parses each file looking for readFile/readFileSync calls where the path argument references src/ (using simple regex)\\n3. Fails with a clear error message: \\\"Test file X reads source file Y. Tests should exercise behavior (import functions, call CLI, make HTTP requests) not scan source code for string patterns.\\\"\\n\\nNo allowlist needed — there are no valid exceptions.\\n\\nThis should run as part of npm test so it catches new static analysis tests before they merge.\\n\\nNote: The project uses Biome (not ESLint), and Biome doesn't support custom rules. A vitest lint test is the right approach — it's the same pattern used for other convention enforcement (see tests/convention-validation.test.ts).\\n\\nThis task is blocked on all E2E migration and deletion tasks completing first.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged PR #575 (tests/lint/no-static-analysis.test.ts) adding CI lint guard against source-scanning tests; removed remaining static-analysis test patterns.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-tasks-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-items-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-inbox-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-meta-validation-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-triage-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-errors-projects-api\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-server-core\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-websocket\",\n      \"@task-e2e-daemon-watcher\",\n      \"@task-delete-static-analysis-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"ci\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJF51MP7P74B0KE93BPKQC3W\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T00:36:04.458Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:57:30.523Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:05:24.188Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:17:32.858Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF5GD8YHVV7SM2ZX9RQJP7K\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:05:06.846Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented CI lint test at tests/lint/no-static-analysis.test.ts to block static-analysis anti-patterns: scans tests/**/*.test.ts for readFile/readFileSync calls that reference src/ or packages/*/src/ and fails with explicit guidance message. Removed existing source-scanning tests to satisfy no-exception rule: deleted tests/stdin-named-handlers.test.ts, removed setup.ts bare-catch static assertion from tests/setup-pipeline-unification.test.ts, and replaced session-create source-comment assertion with behavioral EXIT_CODES.USAGE_ERROR assertion. Verification: npx vitest run tests/lint/no-static-analysis.test.ts tests/session-create.test.ts tests/setup-pipeline-unification.test.ts passed (80/80); npm test currently fails on pre-existing context-sensitive timeouts (batch-exec-engine atomic rollback and ralph/session-budget-integration cleanup tests) when running in ralph session env with KSPEC_SESSION_ID/KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION set.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCQ01EAF79RKFYTMBSZRP1Q\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-shadow-shallow-clone-detection\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Fix shadow branch remote detection in shallow clones\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"remoteBranchExists() uses git show-ref which relies on locally-fetched refs. In shallow clones, kspec-meta refs are never populated, causing init to create a fresh orphan branch instead of attaching to the existing remote one. Fix: use git ls-remote to query remote directly. Also fix initializeShadow to fetch the branch before worktree creation, and update ralph-container entrypoint check.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@shadow-init-remote\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #548. remoteBranchExists() now uses git ls-remote for shallow clone compatibility. AC-4 spec updated to match.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T10:13:01.513Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T10:13:32.379Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T10:21:05.762Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T10:41:18.809Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJCQ9CV7317W85C29TRY0DYR\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T10:18:08.104Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete. Changed remoteBranchExists() from git show-ref to git ls-remote for shallow clone compat. Updated initializeShadow to fetch with refspec (kspec-meta:kspec-meta) and set tracking via git config instead of git branch --set-upstream-to. Added AC-5 test for shallow clones using file:// protocol. Also fixed ralph-container entrypoint to use git ls-remote.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCT38Z5DFJTVH1DJ860PD4P\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-test-bootstrap-link-detection\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add tests for bootstrap link detection\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add unit tests for bootstrap.cjs link detection logic (checkKspecCli). Cover: global kspec not linked, dist not built yet, already linked, symlink resolution on Unix. Extract testable helpers if needed.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@bootstrap-script\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"test\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:07:13.253Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCW37YCFYNRWF1R8P6D5KE1\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-fix-triage-e2e-ac-gaps\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Investigate kspec validate not crediting triage API E2E annotations\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Codex retrospective review of PR #547 found coverage gaps in the triage API E2E tests. MUST-FIX: (1) kspec validate doesn't credit AC annotations in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-triage.spec.ts — likely path/root mismatch. (2) ac-3/ac-4/ac-5 claim coverage but don't verify triage:updates WebSocket broadcast — file marks WS as N/A which conflicts. (3) ac-5 never verifies result_ref for result-producing actions. SHOULD-FIX: (4) @trait-api-endpoint ac-5 (shadow commit) annotated as implicitly covered but no test checks shadow commit occurrence.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-daemon-api\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #552. Bootstrap now always rebuilds dist/ to prevent stale code. Root cause was checkBuild() only checking existence, not freshness.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"e2e\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:42:09.349Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:48:57.047Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:54:12.777Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T12:07:17.141Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJCWETVNFAKFMQ8H3X2NFVHE\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:48:29.173Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Description: kspec validate --completeness reports all own and trait ACs for @triage-daemon-api as uncovered, despite annotations existing in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-triage.spec.ts. Likely a path/root mismatch in scanTestCoverage. Investigate root cause and fix.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJCWMBVTNYB31XDEEG1YAY6Q\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:51:30.426Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Root cause found: bootstrap.cjs checkBuild() only checks if dist/cli/index.js EXISTS, not whether it's stale. When source changes (like adding E2E scan paths to validate.ts) but dist/ already exists from a prior build, bootstrap skips npm run build. The npm-linked kspec binary then runs stale dist/ code. Fix: compare mtime of newest src/ file vs dist/cli/index.js. After local npm run build, all 9 triage ACs + trait ACs are correctly detected.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJCW71YTXH4JG06QN5CKP5FJ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-triage-e2e-behavioral-coverage\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add missing behavioral coverage to triage API E2E tests\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-daemon-api\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-fix-triage-e2e-ac-gaps\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"e2e\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T11:44:14.296Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJD106N5ZQ3VB9T3EV3BHYZK\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-ci-e2e-tests\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Add E2E test job to CI\",\n    \"type\": \"infra\",\n    \"description\": \"Add a separate GitHub Actions job for Playwright E2E tests. Should install Playwright chromium with deps (cache browsers), run npm run test:e2e, and be distinct from the unit test shards. Reference imgen CI pattern for browser caching strategy.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ci\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T13:07:52.613Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDFWAA0883CNHNQ37PYMGNF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:27:53.920Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Automation status set to manual_only: CI configuration requires human judgment on runner resources, caching strategy, and secrets\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"manual_only\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYRZD15F9VGD8N11TR5H0\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-per-role-adapter-selection-for-ralph-loo\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Per-role adapter selection for ralph loop\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add --worker-adapter and --reviewer-adapter flags to ralph CLI for per-role adapter selection.\\n\\n## What to change\\n\\n1. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** (~line 879) — Add two new CLI options: --worker-adapter <id> and --reviewer-adapter <id>. After option parsing (~line 968), resolve two adapters using precedence: role flag > --adapter > default.\\n\\n2. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** — Pass workerAdapter to main iteration spawn (~line 1303) and reviewerAdapter to processPendingReviewTasks() (~line 1158). Wrap-up agent uses workerAdapter.\\n\\n3. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** — Update validation to check both adapters on startup. Deduplicate when same ID (validate once, inject env once). Track injected adapters in a Set.\\n\\n4. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** — Update dry-run output to show both adapter IDs. Record both in session start event metadata.\\n\\n## Precedence\\nworker = --worker-adapter ?? --adapter ?? claude-agent-acp\\nreviewer = --reviewer-adapter ?? --adapter ?? claude-agent-acp\\nwrap-up = worker (always)\\n\\n## How to verify\\n- kspec ralph run --dry-run --worker-adapter codex-acp shows codex-acp for worker\\n- kspec ralph run --dry-run --reviewer-adapter codex-acp shows codex-acp for reviewer\\n- Both invalid adapters cause exit code 3 before session creation\\n- Same adapter ID deduplicates validation and env injection\\n- Session metadata records both adapter IDs\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-per-role-adapters\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #564. Added --worker-adapter and --reviewer-adapter flags with precedence resolution, deduped validation/env injection (including alias normalization for claude-code-acp), per-role adapter routing for worker/reviewer/wrap-up, and 12 tests covering all ACs.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-register-codex-acp-in-adapter-registry\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:48.749Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:25:04.040Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:35:47.745Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:05:21.766Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYRZDGNBX74NF2DFSCEEW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:48.749Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDY1P24K2AVEJPJNWTT9ZVT\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:35:29.861Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented per-role adapter selection:\\n\\n1. Added --worker-adapter and --reviewer-adapter CLI options\\n2. Resolve adapters with precedence: role flag > --adapter > default (claude-agent-acp)\\n3. Validate both adapters at startup, deduplicating when same ID (via Set)\\n4. Inject env for each unique adapter, track previous values per adapter in Map for cleanup\\n5. Worker adapter used for main iteration spawn and wrap-up agent\\n6. Reviewer adapter used for processPendingReviewTasks\\n7. Dry-run output shows both adapter IDs\\n8. Session start event records workerAdapter and reviewerAdapter\\n9. Cleanup (both signal handler and finally block) restores env for all unique adapters\\n\\nTests cover all 12 ACs. 2 pre-existing failures in session-budget-integration.test.ts (tracked by @01KJDSXE).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYSATR96J7FMFSGTG51GQ\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-per-adapter-auto-approve-arguments\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Per-adapter auto-approve arguments\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add per-adapter auto-approve args so --yolo works with any adapter.\\n\\n## What to change\\n\\n1. **src/agents/adapters.ts** — Add optional autoApproveArgs: string[] to AgentAdapter interface. Set for each adapter:\\n   - claude-agent-acp: [\\\"--dangerously-skip-permissions\\\"]\\n   - codex-acp: [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"approval_policy=never\\\", \\\"-c\\\", \\\"sandbox_mode=danger-full-access\\\"]\\n\\n2. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** — Replace hardcoded --dangerously-skip-permissions logic (~line 991) with adapter.autoApproveArgs. Apply per-role (worker gets worker adapter args, reviewer gets reviewer adapter args). When --no-yolo, skip autoApproveArgs entirely.\\n\\n3. **src/agents/spawner.ts** — Ensure spawn args are constructed from a fresh copy of adapter.args + autoApproveArgs to prevent cross-role leakage (adapter objects are registry-backed and mutable).\\n\\n## How to verify\\n- Claude adapter with --yolo passes --dangerously-skip-permissions (existing behavior preserved)\\n- Codex adapter with --yolo passes -c approval_policy=never -c sandbox_mode=danger-full-access\\n- --no-yolo passes no auto-approve args for any adapter\\n- Worker and reviewer auto-approve args are independent (no leakage)\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-adapter-auto-approve\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #563. Replaced hardcoded --dangerously-skip-permissions with per-adapter autoApproveArgs via extraArgs in spawner. 9 tests cover all 4 ACs.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-register-codex-acp-in-adapter-registry\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:49.114Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:48:06.594Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:02:15.479Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:17:25.499Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYSAT8CGF4D804VEAEECD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:49.114Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDW3X8WFVJ982XH0J3FVQVT\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T21:01:45.628Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented per-adapter auto-approve args:\\n- adapters.ts: autoApproveArgs already existed on interface and registrations (from prior task)\\n- spawner.ts: Added extraArgs to SpawnAgentOptions, builds fresh copy of args per spawn\\n- ralph.ts: Replaced hardcoded --dangerously-skip-permissions with adapter.autoApproveArgs, passed as extraArgs to all spawn sites (worker, reviewer subagent, wrap-up agent)\\n- subagent.ts/wrap-up.ts: Added extraArgs to SubagentOptions/WrapUpOptions, forwarded to spawnAndInitialize\\n- acp-mock.js: Added MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ARGS_FILE for verifying command-line args in tests\\n- 9 tests covering all 4 ACs: registry values, extraArgs propagation, no-yolo exclusion, cross-role isolation\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYSNY0TFQB6RFV90HE2X9\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"implement-register-codex-acp-in-adapter-registry\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement Register codex-acp in adapter registry\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Register codex-acp as a first-class adapter and enable Codex env injection.\\n\\n## What to change\\n\\n1. **src/agents/adapters.ts** — Add codex-acp to the ADAPTERS registry with command npx, args [\\\"codex-acp\\\"], and autoApproveArgs (see below). Also add optional autoApproveArgs field to AgentAdapter interface.\\n\\n2. **src/sessions/store.ts** — Uncomment the codex-acp case in injectEnvForAdapter() and removeEnvForAdapter(). The injectCodexEnv() function is already implemented — just wire it into the adapter switch.\\n\\n## Auto-approve args\\ncodex-acp uses config flags: -c approval_policy=\\\"never\\\" -c sandbox_mode=\\\"danger-full-access\\\" for yolo equivalent.\\nclaude-agent-acp uses: --dangerously-skip-permissions\\n\\n## How to verify\\n- resolveAdapter(\\\"codex-acp\\\") returns a registered adapter (not ad-hoc npx fallback)\\n- injectEnvForAdapter with codex-acp writes KSPEC_SESSION_ID to Codex config\\n- removeEnvForAdapter with codex-acp restores previous config state\\n- See tests/session-create.test.ts and tests/ralph.test.ts for patterns\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@codex-acp-adapter-registration\",\n    \"plan_ref\": \"@plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #562. Registered codex-acp adapter, added autoApproveArgs to interface, wired env injection/removal, fixed previousValue propagation caught by Codex review.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:49.470Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:12:15.039Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:20:39.155Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:44:58.769Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDCYSNYVCKH2VNCNC9J1Q9Q\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T16:36:49.470Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"See plan @plan-plan-per-role-adapter-configuration-for-ralph-loop for implementation notes\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDSEJ4M1D9Z69RQ7NSCK19D\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:15:08.948Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete: 1) Added codex-acp to ADAPTERS registry with npx command, codex-acp args, and autoApproveArgs. 2) Added autoApproveArgs field to AgentAdapter interface. Also added autoApproveArgs to claude-agent-acp and claude-code-acp entries. 3) Uncommented codex-acp case in injectEnvForAdapter. 4) Added removeCodexEnv function and wired it into removeEnvForAdapter. 5) Added 4 tests covering all 3 ACs.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDGCEF2MXN9KEMJ2F4S5VVP\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Add batch usage template for agent instructions and CLI example output\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Two parts: (1) New agents-sections template (02-cli-usage.md) documenting batch JSON format, arg rules, invocation methods, and discovery commands. Ships with npm package. (2) CLI enhancement — kspec batch commands <path> to filter output to a single command schema (e.g. kspec batch commands task-set). Documented in the new template. Reduces agent trial-and-error when constructing batch payloads.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-allowed-commands\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #560. Added batch usage template (07-batch-usage.md) and path filter for batch commands CLI.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"cli\",\n      \"docs\",\n      \"dx\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T17:36:42.460Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:20:24.049Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:25:51.504Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:42:57.046Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDK6A610NEHK8GA42GYZ4SA\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T18:25:47.201Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete. Created 07-batch-usage.md template, added [path] filter to batch commands with NOT_FOUND exit code and JSON errors on stdout, added 7 path filter tests + 3 template tests. All ACs covered (ac-filter-by-path, ac-filter-not-found). Full test suite passes (pre-existing ralph flaky test unrelated). AGENTS.md and kspec-agents.md updated.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ0YXVQCR1ZY2ZY80G670Q\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Shadow repair: handle missing /bin/sh — use direct git commands instead of spawning shell, fails on \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec shadow repair` (and other shadow branch operations) fails on systems where `/bin/sh` is not available, such as NixOS or fish-only systems. All git operations in `src/parser/shadow.ts` use `execSync()` and `execAsync()` (which is `promisify(exec)`), both of which default to spawning `/bin/sh` to interpret the command string. **Where**: `src/parser/shadow.ts` — all `execSync()` calls (lines ~154, 170, 189, 584, 595, 614) and all `execAsync()` calls (lines ~841, 863, 882, 909, 933, 1007, 1027, 1030, 1179). The `repairShadow()` function at line 1785 is the primary trigger but the issue affects every git-invoking function in the file. **How**: Replace shell-spawning `exec`/`execSync` with `spawnSync`/`spawn` using `{ shell: false }` (or simply omitting shell). Pass git commands as arrays: `spawnSync('git', ['rev-parse', '--git-dir'], { cwd, stdio })`. This avoids needing `/bin/sh` entirely. The `spawn` import already exists at line 12 but is unused for most operations. For `execAsync` calls, use `child_process.execFile` (which does not use a shell by default) wrapped with `promisify`. **Done when**: (1) All `execSync`/`execAsync` calls in `shadow.ts` use `spawnSync`/`execFileAsync` instead of shell-based execution. (2) `kspec shadow repair` succeeds on a system without `/bin/sh`. (3) All existing shadow tests pass. (4) No string interpolation of git commands (eliminates shell injection risk as a bonus).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@shadow-repair-cmd\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:46.139Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQVZCFA46XS91H4TP27506\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:31.344Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @shadow-repair-cmd spec. Large scope (15+ functions) but spec exists with ACs. Shell portability fix — replace /bin/sh spawns with direct git commands.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ107WAD90WTAVFFQDW0B1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec task patch appears to hang indefinitely — had to kill and use task set + task note as workarou\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec task patch @ref` hangs indefinitely when invoked without piped stdin and without `--data`. The command reads from `process.stdin` using a `for await` loop (line 999-1003 in `src/cli/commands/task.ts`) which blocks forever waiting for input when stdin is a TTY. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/task.ts`, lines 993-1004 — the `else` branch of the `if (options.data)` check. When `--data` is not provided, the code does `for await (const chunk of process.stdin)` which never resolves if stdin is a terminal. **How**: Add TTY detection before attempting to read stdin. If `process.stdin.isTTY` is true and `--data` was not provided, print an error message explaining that either `--data <json>` must be provided or JSON must be piped to stdin, then exit with a validation error. Example: `if (!options.data && process.stdin.isTTY) { error('Provide --data or pipe JSON to stdin'); process.exit(EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED); }`. Alternatively, add a short timeout on stdin reads. **Done when**: (1) Running `kspec task patch @ref` without `--data` and without piped stdin immediately prints a helpful error and exits. (2) `kspec task patch @ref --data '{...}'` still works. (3) `echo '{...}' | kspec task patch @ref` still works. (4) Batch exec engine (`src/cli/batch-exec.ts`) still works with task patch.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@task-patch\",\n    \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:47.484Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:42:16.130Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:44:55.782Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH8VZV37NY5P2HGGM1MAH94\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:42:20.899Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Execution context: add TTY guard in task patch stdin path so interactive runs fail fast instead of hanging; preserve --data and piped-stdin behavior; update CLI tests in tests/task.test.ts and verify batch path remains functional.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH8ZQ3XZ4ATR45B2WNKXR0Q\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:44:23.037Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented stdin TTY guard for task patch: if --data is absent and input is interactive (process.stdin.isTTY or KSPEC_TEST_TTY), command now exits immediately with validation error instead of waiting on stdin. Also treats empty stdin as no patch data. Added integration regressions for piped-stdin success and interactive/no-data fast-fail; verified with npm run build, npx vitest run tests/integration.test.ts -t \\\"Integration: task patch\\\", and npx vitest run tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH90V9G87QJMPGJQ970BMH6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:45:00.080Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #588 (fix/task-patch-tty-guard). Includes TTY no-data guard for task patch + empty-stdin validation and integration tests for piped stdin and interactive fast-fail. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/integration.test.ts -t 'Integration: task patch'; npx vitest run tests/batch-exec-engine.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ11EVH8RKBV4CHZ7R0C89\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix @observations slug ambiguity — kspec validate reports 6 errors for duplicate slug. Pre-existing \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec validate` reports 6 reference errors because the slug `observations` maps to two different items: a spec feature (ULID `01KF1XFBK00000000000000000`, type feature in `modules/meta.yaml`) and a skill (ULID `01KJ51SSZ2NVZGXE32NR5TWPS9`, type skill in `kynetic.meta.yaml`). Any `@observations` reference is ambiguous. 6 references in `modules/meta.yaml` (implements fields) and `project.tasks.yaml` (spec_ref) are affected. **Where**: `.kspec/modules/meta.yaml` — the spec feature item with slug `observations`. `.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` — the skill with id `observations`. The slug collision happens in the reference index (`src/parser/refs.ts`) which treats spec slugs and meta item ids as the same namespace. **How**: Rename the skill id from `observations` to something distinct like `observe` or `capture-observations`, OR rename the spec feature slug. The skill id is less entrenched (it was recently created) so renaming it is lower risk. Update: (1) the skill id in `kynetic.meta.yaml`, (2) any skill file references, (3) the rendered skill in `.claude/skills/`. After the rename, `kspec validate` should report 0 reference errors for this slug. Use `kspec batch` for the meta changes. **Done when**: (1) `kspec validate` no longer reports duplicate slug errors for `@observations`. (2) The skill is still functional under its new id. (3) All 6 previously-ambiguous references resolve correctly. (4) `kspec agents generate` still includes the observations skill.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:48.731Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ12GB09XHW1HVNMC7YJC4\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Ralph PR merge should auto-delete remote branches after merge. Currently accumulates stale branches \",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: After ralph merges PRs via the `pr-review-loop` workflow, remote branches accumulate because the merge step does not include `--delete-branch`. 13 stale branches were found after a single session. **Where**: `.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` — the `pr-review-loop` workflow (id `01KFRX0S3VBZGV72A17E21AB9E`), specifically the merge action step at ~line 750-761 which references `kspec workflow start @pr-review-merge`. Also the `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step (~line 297-300) which says `gh pr merge (prefer merge commit to preserve trailers)`. The release skill at `.claude/skills/release/SKILL.md` line 220 already uses `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch` as a pattern. **How**: Update the `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step content in `kynetic.meta.yaml` to explicitly include `--delete-branch` in the `gh pr merge` command guidance. Change the step from `gh pr merge (prefer merge commit to preserve trailers)` to `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`. This is a meta YAML change — use `kspec` CLI to update the workflow step, or edit the workflow directly. **Done when**: (1) The `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step includes `--delete-branch` in its guidance. (2) `kspec agents generate` regenerated to reflect the change. (3) After a ralph PR merge, the source branch is deleted from the remote.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:49.803Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ139SP70H2H9GNBH8BM72\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec agents generate should include package version in content hash (or add --force flag) so versio\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec agents generate` skips regeneration when content is unchanged, but the staleness check does not include the package version in the content hash. After a version bump (e.g., 0.6.0 to 0.7.0), the generated file header comment is stale, but the hash matches because version is not part of the hash input. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/agents.ts` — the `computeMetaHash()` function (line 125-154) computes a hash from skills, conventions, workflows, and template sections, but does not include the package version. The `generateFreshnessComment()` function (line 160) uses `version` from the package but this is only in the output, not the hash. The skip logic is at ~line 346-348 where `checkAgentStatus()` compares the stored hash. **How**: Add the package `version` string to the hash input in `computeMetaHash()`. Add `data.version = version` (importing `version` from the package, which is already imported at the top of the file for `generateFreshnessComment`). This way, any version bump automatically invalidates the hash and triggers regeneration. Alternatively or additionally, add a `--force` flag to `kspec agents generate` that bypasses the hash check. **Done when**: (1) `computeMetaHash()` includes the package version in its hash computation. (2) After a version bump, `kspec agents generate` regenerates the file instead of skipping. (3) Existing tests in `tests/agents-instruction-gen.test.ts` updated to reflect the new hash behavior. (4) Optionally: `--force` flag added to bypass the hash check entirely.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@agents-cli\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:50.617Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ142M8AM5HAYQBBG12VRS\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec setup should work without CLAUDECODE=1 env var in non-interactive contexts. Either add a --age\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec setup` requires the `CLAUDECODE=1` environment variable (or `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` or `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`) to detect the agent type as `claude-code`. In non-interactive contexts like containerized ralph runners, these env vars may not be available, causing `detectAgent()` to return `unknown` and setup to fail or print manual instructions instead of auto-configuring. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/setup.ts` — the `detectAgent()` function (line 82-100) checks `process.env.CLAUDECODE`, `process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT`, and `process.env.CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. The `registerSetupCommand()` function (line 1638-1655) has options like `--dry-run`, `--author`, `--no-hooks` etc. but no `--agent` flag. The `getSetupStatus()` function (line 774) and the main setup action (line 1345) both call `detectAgent()`. **How**: Add an `--agent <type>` option to `kspec setup` that explicitly specifies the agent type, bypassing `detectAgent()`. Supported values: `claude-code`, `cline`, `cursor`, `windsurf`, `unknown`. When `--agent` is provided, skip detection and use the provided type directly. Also consider a fallback detection: if env vars are absent, check for `~/.claude` directory existence as a weaker signal for `claude-code`. The option should be threaded through to both `runSetup()` and `getSetupStatus()`. **Done when**: (1) `kspec setup --agent claude-code` works without any CLAUDECODE env var set. (2) `kspec setup --status --agent claude-code` reports correct status. (3) `detectAgent()` still works as before when `--agent` is not provided. (4) Invalid `--agent` values are rejected with a clear error. (5) Tests in `tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts` and `tests/setup-pipeline-unification.test.ts` updated.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@enhanced-setup\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:51.412Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1513YJA4PKRTA8CZDE4P\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec task set --priority accepts numbers (1-5) but all documentation, conventions, and plan documen\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec task set --priority` and `kspec task add --priority` only accept raw numbers (1-5), but all documentation, conventions, and plan documents use P1/P2/P3 notation. The error message says 'Priority must be a number between 1 and 5' which is confusing when P-notation is used everywhere else. **Where**: `src/cli/validators.ts` — the `parseIntOption()` function (line 36-64) is used for priority parsing. It calls `Number(value)` which rejects `P1` etc. The priority option is defined in `src/cli/commands/task.ts` at lines 608, 827. The `parseIntOption` is called at lines 287-296 (task set) and 759-767 (task add). **How**: Create a `parsePriority()` wrapper function in `src/cli/validators.ts` that first normalizes P-notation before calling `parseIntOption()`. Implementation: strip a leading case-insensitive `P` prefix if present (`value.replace(/^[Pp]/, '')`), then delegate to `parseIntOption()`. Replace all `parseIntOption(options.priority, { min: 1, max: 5, name: 'Priority' })` calls in `task.ts` with `parsePriority(options.priority)`. Update the option description from 'Priority (1-5)' to 'Priority (1-5 or P1-P5)'. Update the error message to mention both formats. **Done when**: (1) `kspec task set @ref --priority P1` works and sets priority to 1. (2) `kspec task add --priority p3` works (case-insensitive). (3) `kspec task set @ref --priority 2` still works (backward compatible). (4) Invalid values like `P6`, `Px`, `0` are rejected with a clear error mentioning both formats. (5) Tests in `tests/cli-validators.test.ts` cover both formats. (6) CLI help text shows accepted format.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:52.387Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1677X9VQ0DGK550NBGZX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Tests fail when run inside ralph loop due to environment contamination: (1) ralph.test.ts KSPEC_RALP\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: Three tests fail when run inside a ralph loop because they inherit environment variables from the parent ralph process instead of running in a clean env:\\n\\n1. `tests/ralph.test.ts` line ~618: The test asserts `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` is null for non-ralph child processes, but when tests run inside a ralph loop, the env var leaks from the parent process via `...process.env` spread (line 40).\\n\\n2. `tests/session-create.test.ts`: The `kspecJson()` helper parses stdout as JSON, but when KSPEC_SESSION_ID is inherited from ralph, the session-create command emits an \\\"active session\\\" warning to stderr that contaminates the output parsing.\\n\\n3. `tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts`: References a nonexistent `task set-automation` command (the actual command is `task set --automation`).\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `tests/ralph.test.ts` — `runRalph()` helper (lines 27-56), env propagation test (lines 591-619)\\n- `tests/session-create.test.ts` — tests using `kspecJson()` for session creation\\n- `tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts` — the test referencing `set-automation`\\n- `tests/helpers/cli.ts` — the `kspec()` and `kspecJson()` helpers\\n\\n**How**:\\n- In `runRalph()` and test helpers that spawn child processes, explicitly delete `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` and `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` from the env spread unless the test specifically tests those vars. The pattern at line 601-603 already shows the approach.\\n- Apply the same cleanup to the `kspec()` and `kspecJson()` helpers in `tests/helpers/cli.ts` so ALL test invocations are isolated from parent ralph env vars by default.\\n- Fix the `set-automation` reference to use the correct `task set --automation` command syntax.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All three test files pass both standalone (`npm test`) and when run inside a ralph loop\\n- The `kspec()` / `kspecJson()` test helpers strip `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` and `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` from inherited env by default\\n- Tests that need these vars explicitly pass them via the `env` option\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:53.607Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ173NEFK9RFZGRS22VG6M\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Shadow branch index inconsistency: observation @01KJ73ME appeared in search results but failed on ks\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec search` can find observations (e.g., @01KJ73ME) via `loadMetaContext()` which reads the meta.observations array from kynetic.yaml, but `kspec item get` fails for the same reference because the `ReferenceIndex` only indexes spec items and tasks — not meta entities like observations, workflows, conventions, or agents.\\n\\nThis is not a write conflict or index corruption. It is an architectural gap: search and item-get use different resolution paths. Search loads observations from meta context, while item-get only resolves through the ReferenceIndex which does not include meta entities.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/search.ts` — loads observations via `loadMetaContext()` (lines 241-257)\\n- `src/cli/commands/item.ts` — uses `refIndex.resolve()` which only covers spec items\\n- `src/parser/refs.ts` — `ReferenceIndex` class that builds the resolution index\\n- `src/cli/commands/meta.ts` — has dedicated `meta observe get` subcommand for observations\\n\\n**How**:\\nTwo options (pick one):\\n1. **Extend ReferenceIndex** to include meta entities (observations, workflows, agents, conventions) so `item get` can resolve them. This is the deeper fix but has namespace collision risk.\\n2. **Improve error message** in `item get` to suggest `kspec meta observe get @ref` when a ref fails to resolve, since observations have their own dedicated get command. This is lighter and avoids mixing namespaces.\\n\\nOption 2 is recommended: observations already have `kspec meta observe get`, so the real bug is a confusing UX, not missing functionality.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec item get @observation-ref` either resolves the observation or provides a clear error message suggesting `kspec meta observe get @ref`\\n- Alternatively, if extending ReferenceIndex: meta entities are resolvable via `item get` with correct type display\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:54.517Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ17W53F5NN0CWTVSEY53R\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: Ralph loop has no per-iteration timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., a tool call hanging on stdin, like the `kspec batch --commands \\\"\\\"` hang), ralph waits indefinitely. Claude Code's per-bash-command timeout (120s default) does not cover all hang scenarios — an agent can be alive but unresponsive at the ACP protocol level.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` — main loop at line ~1127, the `agent.client.prompt()` call at line ~1373 and the reflection prompt call. These are the two main await points that can hang.\\n- `src/acp/client.ts` — the ACP client that manages the session/prompt lifecycle\\n\\n**How**:\\n- Add a configurable `--iteration-timeout <minutes>` CLI option (default: 20 minutes) to the ralph command registration (line ~868).\\n- Wrap the `agent.client.prompt()` calls in a `Promise.race` with a timeout. On timeout: (1) kill the stuck agent process via `agent.kill()`, (2) log the timeout as a failed iteration, (3) apply the existing retry/failure escalation logic.\\n- The timeout should cover the entire iteration (task-work prompt + optional reflection prompt), not individual prompts, since an iteration is the atomic unit of work.\\n- Consider using `AbortController` / `AbortSignal` if the ACP client supports it, otherwise use `Promise.race` with a timer.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec ralph --iteration-timeout 15` kills a stuck agent after 15 minutes and continues to the next iteration (or exits if max failures reached)\\n- Default timeout is 20 minutes\\n- Timeout events are logged to the session event store with type `iteration.timeout`\\n- Existing retry and failure escalation logic handles timeouts the same as other iteration failures\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:55.301Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQW7RZ6DDS9BNKW8XMDXF4\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:39.935Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @cli-ralph spec. New feature: iteration-level timeout for ralph loop. Spec covers ralph command.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ18VNYYAXETR8WREAJW2X\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"kspec batch --commands '' hangs instead of erroring — empty/missing args should fail fast with a cle\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec batch --commands ''` hangs instead of failing fast. When Commander receives `--commands ''` (empty string), `options.commands` is `''` which is falsy in JavaScript. The source selection logic at `src/cli/commands/batch.ts` line 148 (`else if (options.commands)`) skips the inline path and falls through to `source = { type: 'stdin' }`. The stdin reader at `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 114-124 then blocks forever waiting for input that will never come.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/batch.ts` lines 146-152 — source selection logic\\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 100-126 — `readSource()` stdin path\\n\\n**How**:\\nChange the source selection to check `options.commands !== undefined` instead of truthiness:\\n```typescript\\nif (options.file) {\\n  source = { type: 'file', path: options.file };\\n} else if (options.commands !== undefined) {\\n  source = { type: 'inline', json: options.commands };\\n} else {\\n  source = { type: 'stdin' };\\n}\\n```\\nThis way `--commands ''` takes the inline path and gets caught by `parseBatchInput()` which will fail on `JSON.parse('')` with a clear 'Invalid JSON' error.\\n\\nAlternatively, also add early validation in the inline path: if `options.commands` is empty/whitespace, throw `BatchParseError('Empty --commands value')` before attempting parse.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec batch --commands ''` exits immediately with a clear error (not a hang)\\n- `kspec batch --commands ' '` also fails fast\\n- No regression: `kspec batch --commands '[...]'` still works correctly\\n- Add a test case for empty `--commands` input\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:56.309Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ19N46AK8JQT0KQFQV1KH\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"CLI args should accept both kebab-case and underscore variants (e.g. depends-on and depends_on). Cur\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: Batch command validation rejects underscore variants of argument names (e.g., `depends_on`) even though kebab-case (`depends-on`) and camelCase (`dependsOn`) are accepted. Agents generating JSON batch payloads naturally use underscores, which is the standard JSON/Python naming convention. The error message suggests the kebab form, creating a frustrating feedback loop.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 180-216 — `kebabToCamel()` and `getKnownArgNames()` functions\\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 308-327 — unknown arg validation loop\\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 434-496 — `buildCommandArgv()` which also needs to handle underscore keys when building CLI argv\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Add a `underscoreToKebab()` or `underscoreToCamel()` normalizer alongside `kebabToCamel()`.\\n2. In `getKnownArgNames()`, add underscore variants to the known names set (e.g., for `depends-on`, also add `depends_on`).\\n3. In `buildCommandArgv()`, normalize incoming arg keys before classification — convert underscores to kebab-case before looking up in positionalNameSet and optionMap.\\n4. In the required-args check (lines 330-348), also check underscore variants.\\n\\nA cleaner approach: add a single `normalizeArgKey(key)` function that converts any variant (kebab, camel, underscore) to a canonical form, then use it everywhere.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `{\\\"command\\\": \\\"task set\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@task\\\", \\\"depends_on\\\": [\\\"@dep1\\\"]}}` works in batch mode\\n- All three forms accepted: `depends-on`, `dependsOn`, `depends_on`\\n- Same normalization applies to all options, not just depends_on\\n- Add test cases for underscore variant args in batch validation tests\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:57.124Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1AF125H0FK29HE769R4P\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: Ralph event handler uses a `sessionIterationMap` (Map<string, number>) to attribute late ACP session updates to the correct iteration. However, the current implementation has a race condition: when a new ACP session starts for iteration N+1, late updates from iteration N's session can arrive after `sessionIterationMap.set(newSessionId, N+1)` but the old session's listener may still fire. The `_sid` closure variable in the `on('update')` handler captures the session ID correctly, but there is no cleanup of old listeners when starting a new session.\\n\\nThe Codex review on PR #484 identified that the shared mutable `sessionIterationMap` approach is fragile — a session-scoped listener pattern would be more robust.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1061 — `sessionIterationMap` declaration\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` lines 1305-1337 — the `on('update')` handler that uses `sessionIterationMap.get(_sid)` for iteration lookup\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` line 1369 — where new sessions are registered in the map\\n\\n**How**:\\nTwo approaches (pick one):\\n\\n1. **Session-scoped listeners** (recommended): Instead of one persistent `on('update')` handler, register a new listener per ACP session that captures the iteration number in its closure. Remove the old listener when the session ends or a new one starts. This eliminates the shared mutable map entirely.\\n\\n2. **Cleanup old sessions**: When starting a new ACP session, remove the previous session's entry from `sessionIterationMap` and call `agent.client.off('update', oldHandler)` to prevent stale callbacks. Less clean but simpler delta.\\n\\nBoth approaches should also ensure the translator is reset between iterations (it already creates a fresh translator per retry, but verify per-iteration reset).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- Late updates from a previous ACP session are attributed to the correct iteration (the one that created that session)\\n- No shared mutable state for iteration tracking — either session-scoped closures or explicit cleanup\\n- Existing event logging tests still pass\\n- Event log entries show correct iteration numbers even when sessions overlap\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:57.953Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQVH2H94SY215Y96TMWF0K\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:16.689Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @cli-ralph spec. Ralph internal: session-scoped event listener mapping. Clear scope from enrichment.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1B9C62DT55EK8WK01BP0\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"**What**: When `kspec plan import` runs inside batch mode, non-fatal warnings (e.g., 'no YAML code block in specs section') cause the batch to fail and roll back. The plan-import command uses `warn()` for non-fatal issues and `process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS)` on completion. In batch mode, `process.exit()` is intercepted and throws `BatchExitError`. The exit code 0 is correctly detected as success (line 859 in batch-exec.ts). However, the warnings written to stderr via `warn()` are captured by `OutputCapture` and when the captured output is returned, it may be treated as an error indicator by the batch result processing.\\n\\nThe core issue is that `plan import` calls `process.exit(0)` even on success (line 687 of plan-import.ts). In batch mode, this throws `BatchExitError(0)`, which IS handled as success (batch-exec.ts line 859). But the warnings in captured stderr make the output look like a failure. Additionally, the batch atomic mode may see stderr output as part of the error string when `BatchExitError` code is non-zero for other plan import failures.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts` line 687 — `process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS)` which triggers BatchExitError in batch mode\\n- `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts` lines 124-135 — warning emission for non-fatal parse errors\\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 849-875 — BatchExitError handling in `dispatchCommand()`\\n- `src/cli/batch-context.ts` — OutputCapture that captures both stdout and stderr\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. In `plan-import.ts`, replace the final `process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS)` with a simple `return`. The batch executor expects normal returns for success — only use `process.exit()` for failures. This is the main fix.\\n2. Alternatively, ensure that `dispatchCommand()` in batch-exec.ts distinguishes between stderr warnings and actual errors when a `BatchExitError(0)` is caught — treat exit code 0 as success regardless of captured output content.\\n3. Consider adding a `warnings` field to `BatchCommandResult` so warnings can be reported without marking the command as failed.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec plan import` with warnings runs successfully in batch mode (no rollback)\\n- Warnings are still visible in batch output (not silenced)\\n- Plan import still fails correctly in batch mode for actual errors (YAML parse errors, missing module, etc.)\\n- Add a test case: batch with a plan import that produces warnings should succeed\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:58.796Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1C22TH9SEXXGBYQT8Y3Z\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Plan import --update replaces all ACs instead of merging. When extending an existing spec with a new\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Plan import --update replaces all ACs instead of merging. When extending an existing spec with a new AC via plan import, --update overwrites acceptance_criteria entirely. Need AC-merge strategy: append new AC IDs, preserve existing ones. Encountered during spec-plan for session-log-show ac-10.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:59.586Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ8ZD10EG4Z7MHEAHWBMAT\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:37:08.769Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When `kspec plan import --update` encounters an existing spec, it replaces the entire `acceptance_criteria` array instead of merging. If a spec already has ac-1 through ac-9 and a plan adds ac-10, --update overwrites all ACs with only what the plan document contains, losing ac-1 through ac-9.\\n\\n**Where**: `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts` lines 271-303 (the --update branch). The update logic builds a `Partial<SpecItemInput>` and sets `updates.acceptance_criteria = spec.acceptance_criteria` (line 296), passed to `updateSpecItem()` in `src/parser/yaml.ts` line 1522. `updateSpecItem` does direct property assignment (`targetObj[key] = value` at line 1560) with no merge logic.\\n\\n**How**: Implement an AC merge strategy in the update path. When `updates.acceptance_criteria` is set and the existing item already has ACs:\\n1. Index existing ACs by their `id` field (e.g., \\\"ac-1\\\", \\\"ac-2\\\")\\n2. For each AC in the plan update: if an AC with the same `id` exists, replace it; otherwise append it\\n3. Preserve existing ACs whose IDs are not in the update set\\nBest done in `plan-import.ts` before calling `updateSpecItem`, since general updateSpecItem callers may want full replacement semantics.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec plan import --update` with a plan that adds one new AC to an existing spec preserves all pre-existing ACs and appends the new one\\n- A plan that modifies an existing AC (same id) updates that AC in place while preserving others\\n- Tests cover: append-only new AC, update existing AC by id, mixed append+update, no ACs in plan (preserves existing), empty existing ACs (creates all from plan)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1CTV35WDA9G51NEH943K\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Agents should check plan_ref when starting tasks. If a task has plan_ref, run kspec plan get @plan-r\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Agents should check plan_ref when starting tasks. If a task has plan_ref, run kspec plan get @plan-ref to read implementation notes, algorithm details, and context. Update task-work skill and task-work-loop workflow to include this step. Plans are the right place for rich implementation context instead of cramming it into task notes.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:00.379Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ9E2V7MF4XRKW0MQQC59X\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:37:23.804Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When agents start a task that has a `plan_ref` field, they should automatically retrieve the plan to get implementation notes, algorithm details, and design context. Currently the task-work skill and task-work-loop workflow do not mention checking plan_ref. Plans are the intended home for rich implementation context rather than cramming it into task descriptions or notes.\\n\\n**Where**: \\n- `templates/skills/task-work/SKILL.md` — Step 3 \\\"Start Task\\\" section (line 86-90) needs a substep: \\\"If task has plan_ref, run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` to read implementation notes\\\"\\n- Task-work-loop workflow definition in `.kspec/` (the workflow YAML) — add the same step\\n- `src/cli/commands/task.ts` — the `task get` output already shows `plan_ref` when present; the `task start` command could optionally print a hint like \\\"This task has a plan: run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` for implementation context\\\"\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Update `templates/skills/task-work/SKILL.md` step 3 to add: \\\"If `kspec task get @ref` shows a `plan_ref`, run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` to read implementation notes and design context before starting work.\\\"\\n2. Update the task-work-loop workflow to include the same check in its automated flow\\n3. Optionally enhance `kspec task start` in `src/cli/commands/task.ts` to print an info message when the started task has a non-null plan_ref\\n4. Run `kspec agents generate` after template changes\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- The task-work skill documents checking plan_ref when starting tasks\\n- The task-work-loop workflow includes plan context retrieval\\n- Agents following the skill will automatically get plan context when a task has plan_ref\\n- `kspec agents generate` produces updated kspec-agents.md\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQVPYHQ56GVPJH0EKJ6TWV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:22.705Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Infra: Workflow/skill documentation change. Agents check plan_ref when starting tasks. No code change needed, skill template update.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1DQMCBX32KDVWBJBF8W1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ4SNEC), short refs like @01KJ4SNE fail. kspec already has a shortest-unique-ID utility — this should be used anywhere refs are displayed (triage list, task list, inbox list, promote result_ref, etc.) so that presented refs are always unambiguous and copy-pasteable into subsequent commands.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:01.300Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQA0MV956KKZREMG980AE6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:37:42.812Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g., 01KJ4SNE9... and 01KJ4SNEC...), the default 8-character short ref `@01KJ4SNE` is ambiguous and fails to resolve. The `ReferenceIndex.shortUlid()` method (in `src/parser/refs.ts` line 310) already computes the minimum unique prefix, but many places in the codebase use a hardcoded `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` instead. There are 69 occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` across 19 files.\\n\\n**Where**: All places that format ULID refs for display need to use `shortUlid()` instead of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)`. Key files with hardcoded slicing:\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` (14 occurrences) — triage list, record, act, get, start\\n- `src/cli/commands/inbox.ts` (9 occurrences) — inbox list, add, promote\\n- `src/cli/commands/item.ts` (6 occurrences) — item list, get, add\\n- `src/cli/commands/plan.ts` (9 occurrences) — plan list, get\\n- `src/cli/commands/search.ts` (4 occurrences) — search results\\n- `src/cli/commands/session/context.ts` (4 occurrences) — session context display\\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` (1 occurrence) — promote result ref\\n- `src/parser/validate.ts` (8 occurrences) — validation output\\n- Several other files with 1-3 occurrences each\\n\\nThe `ReferenceIndex` is already available in most of these contexts (it's built during `initContext()` or `buildIndexes()`).\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. For each file, replace `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` with `index.shortUlid(_ulid)` where a ReferenceIndex is in scope\\n2. For files where no index is available, either thread the index through or create a lightweight shortening utility\\n3. For triage records (which aren't indexed in the main ReferenceIndex), consider building a local index or a dedicated triage ULID shortener\\n4. Ensure that refs displayed by any list/get/result command are always copy-pasteable into subsequent commands without ambiguity\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- No occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` remain in display-facing code paths\\n- All displayed refs (triage list, task list, inbox list, search results, promote result_ref, etc.) use `shortUlid()` or equivalent\\n- A test with two items sharing an 8-character ULID prefix shows that displayed refs are still unique and resolvable\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1EKVV4V60V7WT6DCK3H3\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently pro\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently promoted items stay in inbox requiring manual cleanup. Consider --consume flag or making deletion the default for promote (with snapshot preserved in triage record).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:02.203Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQAHM5SX18W9F5V0ET02G6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:00.197Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When `kspec triage act` executes a \\\"promote\\\" action, it creates a new task from the inbox item but leaves the original inbox item in the inbox. This requires a separate manual `kspec inbox delete` step to clean up, which is tedious and easy to forget. The inbox item's text is already preserved in the triage record's `item_snapshot` field, so the original is not needed for audit trail purposes.\\n\\n**Where**: \\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` lines 54-74 — the `promote` case in `executeTriageAction()`. Currently creates the task and returns, but never calls `deleteInboxItem()` for the promoted item.\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` lines 235-289 — the `triage act` command handler. This is where the `--consume` flag would be parsed and passed to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n- The `delete` and `duplicate` cases (lines 77-90, 117-130) already call `deleteInboxItem()` — the promote case can follow the same pattern.\\n\\n**How**: Two reasonable approaches:\\n1. **Flag approach**: Add `--consume` flag to `kspec triage act` that deletes the inbox item after promote. Pass it through `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n2. **Default behavior**: Make deletion the default for promote (since the snapshot is preserved in the triage record), with a `--keep` flag to opt out.\\n\\nRecommendation: Option 2 (delete by default) is cleaner since every promoted item has its text preserved in `item_snapshot`. The `--keep` flag is the escape hatch. The `delete` and `duplicate` cases already delete inbox items as their default behavior, so promote doing the same is consistent.\\n\\nImplementation:\\n1. Add `consume` option to `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` (default true for promote)\\n2. In the `promote` case of `executeTriageAction()`, after creating the task, call `deleteInboxItem()` for `record.inbox_ref` unless consume is false\\n3. Add `--keep` flag to `kspec triage act` command that sets `consume: false`\\n4. Update dry-run output to mention deletion\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec triage act <ref>` on a promote record creates the task AND deletes the inbox item\\n- `kspec triage act <ref> --keep` creates the task but preserves the inbox item\\n- Dry-run output mentions that the inbox item would be deleted\\n- The `item_snapshot` in the triage record still contains the original text for audit trail\\n- Tests cover: promote with deletion (default), promote with --keep, dry-run output\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1FCWDDH5FM5JKSWNYVBX\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserv\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI: persist all filter state and current view in URL query params so refreshing the page preserves state. Applies to all list/filter pages (triage, inbox, tasks, etc).\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@web-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.004Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQB2J9SKA1QNC3SG3NN8WF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:17.546Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: Web UI pages lose their filter state when the browser refreshes. For example, filtering tasks by status=in_progress or triage by tag=cli is lost on reload. Filter state should be persisted in URL query parameters so that refreshing preserves the view, and URLs are shareable/bookmarkable.\\n\\n**Where**: The tasks page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte`) already partially implements URL-based filters — it reads from `$page.url.searchParams` (line 39-47) via the `filterParams` derived value. However, the triage page (`packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) uses local `$state` variables (`filterTag`, `filterStatus` at lines 43-44) that are NOT synced to URL params. Other list pages (items, inbox) likely have the same issue.\\n\\nKey files to update:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte` — filterTag and filterStatus need URL param sync\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte` — check if filters use URL params\\n- Any other list/filter pages under `packages/web-ui/src/routes/`\\n\\n**How**: Follow the pattern already established in the tasks page:\\n1. Read initial filter values from `$page.url.searchParams` (from `$app/stores`)\\n2. When a filter changes, use `goto()` (from `$app/navigation`) to update URL params without a full page reload: `goto(\\\\`?status=\\\\${filterStatus}&tag=\\\\${filterTag}\\\\`, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true })`\\n3. Use `$derived` to compute filter values from URL params (like tasks page does)\\n4. This approach gives: URL persistence, back/forward navigation, shareable links\\n\\nFor the triage page specifically:\\n- Replace `let filterTag = $state('')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('tag')`\\n- Replace `let filterStatus = $state('all')` with reading from `$page.url.searchParams.get('status')`\\n- Add `goto()` calls when filters change\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- All list/filter pages read initial state from URL query params\\n- Changing a filter updates the URL without full page reload\\n- Refreshing the page preserves filter state\\n- Browser back/forward navigates between filter states\\n- The triage page URL shows filters like `?status=untriaged&tag=cli`\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWG9550XY4Y8F7V6W5W47\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:48.645Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @web-ui module. URL state persistence for filter/view params across all list pages.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1G6HBSJRXVSWEWQ9W9E4\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). Currently no way to filter triage records by action.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@interactive-triage-ui\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:03.825Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQBJ4QTDMCZJ4NAY7B1KGP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:33.495Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The triage page has status and tag filters (lines 326-347 of `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`) but no way to filter triage records by their action type (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate). When reviewing triage history, users often want to see \\\"all promote decisions\\\" or \\\"all spec-gap findings\\\" without scrolling through mixed results.\\n\\n**Where**: `packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte`:\\n- Existing filters: `filterStatus` (all/untriaged/triaged/acted_on) at line 44, `filterTag` at line 43\\n- Filter UI: lines 324-347 (the filter controls div with data-testid=\\\"triage-filters\\\")\\n- Filtered items computation: `filteredItems` derived at lines 78-96 — currently filters by tag and status only\\n- The `TriageAction` type includes: promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, duplicate (defined in `$lib/types/triage`)\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. Add a new `filterAction` state variable: `let filterAction = $state<TriageAction | ''>('')`\\n2. Add a new `<select>` element in the filters div (alongside status and tag filters) with options for each action type\\n3. Add action filtering to the `filteredItems` derived computation:\\n   ```\\n   if (filterAction) {\\n     items = items.filter((i) => i.record?.action === filterAction);\\n   }\\n   ```\\n4. Include the action filter in the `$effect` that resets `currentIndex` when filters change (line 296-302)\\n5. If implementing URL state persistence (task @01KJDQ1F), also sync this filter to URL params\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- A dropdown/select control for triage action type appears in the filter bar\\n- Selecting \\\"promote\\\" shows only items with promote decisions\\n- Selecting \\\"spec-gap\\\" shows only spec-gap items\\n- The empty/default option shows all items (no action filter)\\n- Changing the filter resets the card navigation index to 0\\n- E2E test covers filtering by action type\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQWRKV7J9BSC3BY2NNPNG8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:57.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @interactive-triage-ui spec. Add filter controls for triage action types on triage page.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJDSXEME66TYKVVGGFW6PYT2\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix test failures after v0.7.0 version bump\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"5 tests failing across 3 files after the v0.7.0 bump: (1) tests/claude-plugin-registry.test.ts - checkMarketplaceHealth returns version-mismatch instead of healthy, plugin files still at 0.6.0. (2) tests/package-distribution.test.ts (2 failures) - plugin.json and marketplace.json still show 0.6.0, tests expect 0.7.0. (3) tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts (2 failures) - ralph loop times out waiting for completion marker, likely unrelated to version bump, may be a race condition or mock issue. The plugin version failures are likely fixed by regenerating plugin distribution files. The ralph budget tests need investigation.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"testing\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T20:23:16.878Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE03R4EZDVZS2ZHHEE4WJ81\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Verify and fix codex-acp adapter integration for ralph\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Several issues identified with the codex-acp adapter that prevent it from working correctly with ralph:\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\n### 1. CRITICAL: Env injection writes to wrong config file\\ninjectCodexEnv() in src/sessions/store.ts writes KSPEC_SESSION_ID to ~/.codex/config.json using JSON format. But Codex CLI reads ~/.codex/config.toml (TOML format). The injection has no effect — Codex never sees the session ID.\\n\\nFix: Rewrite injectCodexEnv to read/write ~/.codex/config.toml using TOML format. The key path is shell_environment_policy.set.KSPEC_SESSION_ID. Same for removeCodexEnv.\\n\\n### 2. Auto-approve args may use wrong config keys\\nThe adapter registers these auto-approve args: -c approval_policy=\\\"never\\\" and -c sandbox_mode=\\\"danger-full-access\\\". But codex-acp help shows sandbox_permissions (array), and the config file uses trust_level. Need to verify which keys codex-acp actually accepts and what values produce full auto-approve behavior.\\n\\n### 3. No integration test with real codex-acp\\nAll tests use mock ACP. No test verifies that ralph can actually spawn and communicate with @zed-industries/codex-acp. At minimum, a smoke test that spawns codex-acp and checks ACP handshake would catch protocol mismatches.\\n\\n### 4. Package name fix pending (PR #565)\\nThe adapter registry had codex-acp instead of @zed-industries/codex-acp. Fix is in PR #565, pending merge.\\n\\n## How to verify\\n- kspec ralph run --dry-run --adapter codex-acp shows correct package name\\n- kspec ralph run --max-loops 1 --adapter codex-acp completes one iteration successfully\\n- Session ID reaches kspec subprocesses inside the codex agent\\n- Auto-approve args produce no permission prompts during ralph loop\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #566. Fixed codex env injection to use ~/.codex/config.toml (TOML) instead of config.json (JSON). Added smol-toml dependency, updated all tests, added round-trip preservation test, fixed pre-existing adapter.args assertion, tightened spec AC.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"bug\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:11:34.669Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:13:52.039Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:56:57.626Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:11:57.790Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE2P4YDHZ798YTGWZHX3CF0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T22:56:34.766Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Fixed config.json → config.toml for codex env injection. Added smol-toml dependency. Updated all 7 codex tests + added round-trip preservation test + fixed pre-existing adapter.args assertion (PR #565 aftermath). Auto-approve args confirmed correct via Codex config schema. 67/67 session-create tests pass. Full suite: 155/156 files pass (1 pre-existing flaky integration test unrelated).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE3T75E2F7KYBT7Q89SV5VJ\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Harden Codex environment detection for setup and setup-status\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Codex detection is currently brittle and inconsistent across setup paths.\\n\\nIn this Codex environment, `kspec setup` falls back to unknown because setup detection in `src/cli/commands/setup.ts` only checks `CODEX_SANDBOX`, while active sessions can expose other stable markers such as `CODEX_THREAD_ID`.\\n\\nSeparately, `src/parser/setup-status.ts` uses a different detector that does not recognize Codex at all, so setup and status/doctor can disagree.\\n\\nScope:\\n- Expand setup detection to treat `CODEX_THREAD_ID` as a primary high-confidence Codex signal, while keeping `CODEX_SANDBOX` support for backward compatibility.\\n- Add additional Codex fallbacks/supporting signals if needed to improve robustness without increasing false positives.\\n- Align setup-status/doctor detection with the same Codex signal model and confidence semantics.\\n- Add tests that cover Codex detection when `CODEX_THREAD_ID` is present and `CODEX_SANDBOX` is absent, plus status/setup consistency checks.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #568. Unified setup/setup-status agent detection via shared src/parser/agent-detection.ts, with CODEX_THREAD_ID and CODEX_SANDBOX high-confidence Codex detection plus medium-confidence CODEX_CI/CODEX_MANAGED_BY_NPM fallback; added regression coverage for CODEX_THREAD_ID+GH_TOKEN precedence and setup/status consistency. Infra task (spec_ref null), targeted validation and CI test shards passed.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"setup\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"detection\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:17:00.000Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:08:51.708Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:09:04.801Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:20:52.197Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE5NK4CTQFR2ZWNN55P4N2Q\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:48:42.252Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented unified agent detection model and switched both setup paths to use it. Added shared src/parser/agent-detection.ts with Codex detection priority: CODEX_THREAD_ID (high), CODEX_SANDBOX (high, backward-compatible), and CODEX_CI/CODEX_MANAGED_BY_NPM fallback (medium). Updated src/cli/commands/setup.ts and src/parser/setup-status.ts to consume shared detection semantics. Added tests in tests/agent-detection.test.ts covering CODEX_THREAD_ID without CODEX_SANDBOX, backward compatibility with CODEX_SANDBOX, and setup/setup-status consistency for medium-confidence Codex fallback signals. Verification: vitest new + related suites passed (agent-detection, enhanced-setup, parser/doctor). kspec validate currently fails due unrelated pre-existing repo-wide reference/alignment/completeness issues.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE5P8VH76H46VK36PCGDWXW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:49:04.497Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Follow-up verification: fixed AgentType compatibility in setup.ts by adding cursor/windsurf literals so shared detector return type is assignable. Re-ran pnpm tsc --noEmit and tests/agent-detection.test.ts; both pass.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE6BQWYQ9JD8QT5MNZQKWFM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:00:48.030Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Opened PR #568 with unified Codex detection changes and tests: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/568. Task submitted for review.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE6QTND1JFZABXECVDBW56C\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:07:24.077Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Codex detection precedence bug (CODEX_THREAD_ID can be overshadowed by GH_TOKEN/COPILOT_MODEL) and missing regression test; npm test gate not green.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE6T45PZTGWMGCGW8VTHJ7X\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:08:39.350Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Addressed PR MUST-FIX feedback: moved codex detection precedence ahead of copilot markers in shared detector and added regression test for CODEX_THREAD_ID+GH_TOKEN coexistence. Verification: tests/agent-detection.test.ts and tsc --noEmit pass. Pushed commit 234bab50 to PR #568.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE46AQZHKVQMVWWCWKGH2P3\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Make git root/shadow detection resilient to restricted runtimes\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Issue: In the Codex execution runtime, Node shell-based git calls (execSync with string commands like \\\"git rev-parse --show-toplevel\\\") can fail with spawnSync /bin/sh EPERM even when git itself is available. Impact: getGitRoot() and related checks return false negatives, kspec treats repo as non-git/non-shadow, and writes can fall back to root-level files (for example project.tasks.yaml) instead of .kspec worktree paths. Findings: (1) kspec shadow status returned Not a git repository in this runtime while user environment returned healthy shadow JSON. (2) Running getGitRoot() through parser returned null before fix. (3) Task add created an untracked root project.tasks.yaml due to shadow detection failure. Why: the implementation depended on shell invocation semantics instead of direct process execution, which is fragile in sandboxed/restricted runtimes. Proposal: standardize git invocations in detection-critical paths to direct argv-based spawn/execFile style calls, add regression tests that simulate shell-unavailable execution behavior, and audit other shell-form git calls that can influence path resolution.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #567. Replaced shell-string git detection calls in shadow parser with argv-based sync git invocation () via shared runGitSync helper; updated isGitRepo/getGitRoot/branchExists to avoid /bin/sh dependency in restricted runtimes. Verified CI green and runtime behavior via kspec shadow status/getGitRoot; infra task had no spec_ref so AC coverage gate was N/A.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"shadow\",\n      \"portability\",\n      \"runtime\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:22:53.567Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:26:58.084Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:26:59.112Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:34:56.989Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE46FMZK4P8MB71JJ0J1Z5M\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:22:58.591Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@codex\",\n        \"content\": \"Investigation summary: reproduced mismatch where kspec shadow status failed in Codex runtime but succeeded in user shell. Root cause is shell-form Node git execution failing under restricted runtime (/bin/sh EPERM), which made getGitRoot/isGitRepo/branchExists return false negatives and caused non-shadow fallback writes. Confirmed by direct module probe (getGitRoot returned null before patch) and by root project.tasks.yaml creation from task add before fix.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE4WW318T9VXFJXR70EQRFZ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:35:12.225Z\",\n        \"author\": \"chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Completion clarification: argv-based git invocation uses spawnSync via runGitSync; prior completion reason rendered empty parentheses due shell escaping.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE5A53YPYHZ4M0K2G4PEC0X\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Investigate task lifecycle commands leaving shadow changes staged without auto-commit\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"What: during this session, task lifecycle operations updated `.kspec/project.tasks.yaml` but left changes staged in the shadow worktree instead of producing the expected automatic commit, requiring a manual `git commit` in `.kspec`. Where: task transition flow (`task start/submit/complete`) and shared shadow commit helper integration. How: reproduce with a minimal command sequence, identify when commitIfShadow/shadowAutoCommit is skipped or bypassed, and ensure transitions consistently auto-commit shadow changes. Add regression test covering submit path and staged-index state checks. Done when: task lifecycle commands that mutate shadow state always result in committed shadow changes (no lingering staged diff) unless explicitly in a dry-run or documented exception mode.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"shadow\",\n      \"task-workflow\",\n      \"reliability\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:42:27.454Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE5A565T4K1JZ5XJ5860FH1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Add platform override for skill install-core to support Codex .agents output\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"What: `kspec skill install-core` currently relies on environment auto-detection and has no explicit platform selector. In Codex-misdetection scenarios, it installs/updates `.claude/skills` instead of `.agents/skills`, which blocks intended Codex skill delivery. Where: skill install-core command and platform resolution path used by core skill rendering/install. How: add `--platform <claude-code|codex>` (or equivalent explicit target) for install-core; when set to codex, force install to `.agents/skills` regardless of detection. Keep current auto-detect default for backward compatibility. Add tests for codex forced output path and default behavior. Done when: running `kspec skill install-core --platform codex` writes/updates `.agents/skills/*` and does not require Codex env detection to be correct.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": null,\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skills\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"cli\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T23:42:27.525Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:09.321Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:12.117Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:45.630Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE86X8EY9R143SVPK7M0SR0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:33:06.830Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Investigation (2026-02-27): install-core currently has no explicit platform selector. registerSkillInstallCommands defines install-core options as --force/--dry-run only (src/cli/commands/skill-install.ts). Skill metadata is written directly from core manifest platforms (skillData uses coreSkill.platforms), and setup path uses platforms: coreSkill.platforms || [claude-code] (src/cli/commands/setup.ts). This confirms a codex override flag is currently missing in both direct install-core and setup-driven core install paths.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE8R7ZBR8G0A02J40MD0M4G\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:42:34.860Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented install-core platform targeting (2026-02-27): added --platform <claude-code|codex> option to kspec skill install-core. Without override, platform now auto-detects from agent env (codex-cli -> codex, otherwise claude-code) for backward-compatible default behavior. Core skills are rendered immediately to resolved platform during install-core, so --platform codex writes .agents/skills/kspec-*/SKILL.md independent of env detection.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJECGBK2BFC2FSVFDGD3VX85\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:10.722Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation delivered in PR #569 (branch fix/codex-core-skill-platform-awareness): added install-core platform override and codex-targeted render path assertions; pending review with linked PR checks now green.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJERKFAZKQTMEC3B07Q757EA\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:35.775Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Merged via PR #569 on 2026-02-27 (merge commit 7042139b); install-core --platform override is live.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE7BXBNNFYQ5R05T8DCEZM6\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Enable core skill install/render path for codex\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Root cause: core skills are defined as claude-only, so codex is never targeted.\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- templates/skills/manifest.yaml declares every core skill with platforms: [claude-code].\\n- skill install-core persists platforms directly from core manifest (src/cli/commands/skill-install.ts), and setup pipeline install has a claude-code fallback (src/cli/commands/setup.ts).\\n- setup render pipeline only dispatches renderers from each skill.platforms value; no codex platform in meta means codex renderer is never invoked.\\n- claude-code core skills are intentionally skipped as plugin-provided in claude renderer, so current render result is all plugin-provided skips and no codex rows.\\n\\nImpact:\\n- In Codex environments, running skill install-core/setup does not produce .agents/skills/kspec-*/ SKILL.md outputs for core skills.\\n\\nTracking scope (no implementation in this task creation):\\n- Define expected platform strategy for core skills in Codex (manifest/platform defaults and migration behavior).\\n- Update install-core/setup install path so core skill meta includes codex where intended.\\n- Add regression tests that assert codex core skills are rendered/available after install-core + render/setup.\\n- Verify claude plugin-provided behavior remains unchanged.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": null,\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skills\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"install-core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:18:22.197Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:35:16.481Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:02.326Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:42.802Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE86X9X7XWBQ87BRE6T0KMC\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:33:06.877Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Investigation (2026-02-27): reproduced codex gap in this repo. kspec setup --dry-run --json (detected codex-cli high confidence) reports Render skills: 11 plugin-provided with no rendered skill IDs, and kspec skill render --json shows only claude-code plugin-provided skips. templates/skills/manifest.yaml currently marks all core skills as claude-code only. Because renderSkillsForSetup iterates skill.platforms, codex renderer is never invoked for core skills.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE8F7XBKDG47VBDQRH5S3AB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:37:39.883Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented codex core-skill install/render path (2026-02-27): updated templates/skills/manifest.yaml so all core skills target both claude-code and codex; setup render fallback message now platform-neutral; added regression tests in tests/core-skill-install.test.ts (install-core + skill render creates .agents/skills/kspec-help and keeps claude core plugin-provided) and tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts (setup in codex env renders core skills to codex output). Verified with npm run build plus vitest runs: core-skill-install, enhanced-setup, core-skill-update, setup-pipeline-unification, core-skill-namespace all passing.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJECGKGR5GZSP3FD9AJ0BTSH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:18.840Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"PR #569 updated and re-reviewed on 2026-02-27; CI passing on head dba33943; task moved to pending_review.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJERKCJVT1G3PA72NAX8MVZY\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:32.955Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Merged via PR #569 on 2026-02-27 (merge commit 7042139b); codex core install/render path is live.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJE7N3QDCV5GDJKKFE9VQ3W5\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Make core skill cross-references platform-aware (Claude/Codex)\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Core skill content currently uses Claude-style invocation references like `/kspec:task-work`, `/kspec:plan`, etc. In Codex environments this is ambiguous/non-native and can mislead users.\\n\\nDecision needed:\\n- Option A: maintain separate skill variants per platform (e.g., Codex-specific SKILL.md variants).\\n- Option B: keep shared skill content but express cross-references in a platform-neutral or multi-platform form (e.g., include both Claude and Codex invocation forms, such as `/kspec:task-work` and `$task-work`).\\n\\nScope for follow-up implementation:\\n- Define canonical invocation guidance for each supported platform.\\n- Update core skill templates to use platform-aware cross-references.\\n- Ensure rendered outputs preserve correct guidance per platform renderer.\\n- Add tests to prevent regressions (e.g., no Claude-only invocation syntax in Codex-rendered core skills unless explicitly dual-formatted).\\n\\nOut of scope for this tracking task creation: no implementation changes now.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": null,\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skills\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"docs\",\n      \"platform\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:23:23.629Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:47:34.749Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:03.769Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:44.218Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE86XA7G73YT1Q8V613YQQQ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:33:06.888Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Investigation (2026-02-27): core skill content currently contains many Claude-form invocations (/kspec:task-work, /kspec:plan, etc.) in templates/skills/*/SKILL.md. No codex-specific variant pipeline is present for core templates, so codex-rendered output would carry the same references. Related assumptions also appear in parser/config defaults and ralph constants (/kspec:task-work, /kspec:reflect, /kspec:review), so platform-aware guidance likely needs a consistent policy across templates + generated docs + config defaults.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE956KMW4YYXMFW5W3TPF19\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:49:39.444Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented platform-aware core skill references for Codex (2026-02-27): codex renderer now namespaces core skill frontmatter name as kspec-<id> (matching codex directory naming) and applies render-time conversion of Claude-style references /kspec:<id> -> -<id> in rendered SKILL.md body. This keeps shared template source while producing codex-native invocation guidance.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJE95CCSKZEN13XVMVPK8RGF\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T00:49:45.369Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Added regression tests: tests/skill-rendering.test.ts verifies core codex skills render name: kspec-<id> and rewrite /kspec:* references to -*; updated install/setup codex assertions in tests/core-skill-install.test.ts and tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts to expect namespaced codex names. Validation passed across skill-rendering, core-skill-install, enhanced-setup, core-skill-namespace, and core-skill-update suites.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEA53YN88QYHB8R4PE20DDV\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:07:05.301Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Review clarification (2026-02-27): Codex core-skill cross-reference target remains namespaced invocation form (-<id>) to match codex frontmatter naming (kspec-<id>). The temporary /kspec:<id> -> -<id> adjustment was reverted; renderer now keeps -* conversion and scopes rewriting to core skills only to avoid mutating non-core codex content.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEAVR8EHM9K90N4FW0X55WH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:19:26.990Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented portable skill reference tokens end-to-end (2026-02-27): core skill templates now use {skill:<id>} in SKILL.md and triage docs; renderer resolves tokens per platform and origin (Claude: /kspec:<id> for core, /<id> for non-core; Codex: -<id> for core, $<id> for non-core). Supporting markdown directories (docs/references) are transformed during render with idempotent diff/copy checks preserved. Legacy codex core /kspec:<id> rewrite remains as compatibility fallback.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJECGMZ03J8B90EQAZC895ZW\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:20.320Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"PR #569 updated with portable {skill:<id>} token resolution across SKILL.md and supporting markdown; CI passing on head dba33943; task moved to pending_review.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJECH6JT5SMRHS3NRZSXWYE5\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T01:48:38.362Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Correction (2026-02-27): Codex invocation mapping in this task is core -> -<id>, non-core -> $<id>. Some earlier notes displayed '-' due shell interpolation when posting text; implementation/tests/PR use the '$' forms.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJERKDZ4DX2W6PNJAZMRFS7G\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:19:34.372Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Merged via PR #569 on 2026-02-27 (merge commit 7042139b); portable {skill:<id>} reference resolution across SKILL and supporting markdown is live.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJERMMMBGRHY29RFFW92GT0R\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T05:20:13.963Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Final correction (2026-02-27): Codex invocation mapping is core -> $kspec-<id>, non-core -> $<id>; Claude mapping is core -> /kspec:<id>, non-core -> /<id>.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEWKGDK8YRGGF7CEXX0W33H\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Seed Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames with kspec-agents.md\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"What: Ensure Codex project config includes kspec-agents.md in project_doc_fallback_filenames so AGENTS.md fallback discovery can load bundled kspec instructions. Where: setup/install path that currently writes Codex config.toml entries (and/or setup seeding for codex-cli). How: parse ~/.codex/config.toml safely, merge kspec-agents.md into project_doc_fallback_filenames idempotently, preserve existing fields/order where possible, and support dry-run semantics used by setup/install-core. Add regression tests for create, merge, idempotent re-run, and invalid TOML failure handling. Done when: running kspec setup (codex-cli) and kspec skill install-core --platform codex leaves ~/.codex/config.toml with project_doc_fallback_filenames containing kspec-agents.md without clobbering existing config.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #570. Seeded Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames with kspec-agents.md in setup/install-core with tests and AC alignment.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"codex\",\n      \"skills\",\n      \"setup\",\n      \"config\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:29:31.187Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:34:28.412Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:57:32.837Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:58:29.499Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEWWMCXH1FFB3TX8QZNAYX4\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:34:30.173Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames seeding: added shared src/lib/codex-config.ts helper and wired setup memory seeding + skill install-core codex paths to ensure kspec-agents.md is present idempotently, with invalid TOML safety and dry-run behavior. Added regression coverage in tests/cli/setup-seeding.test.ts, tests/core-skill-install.test.ts, and tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEXSA9AJVG4B2CTQT37ZBTZ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:50:10.091Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Addressed PR feedback by adding @new-project-bootstrapping ac-3 for Codex fallback seeding and annotating implementation/tests to AC refs (commit c0268b66).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF06NRBB8EHQ6VGA8AZ8PAY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Close shadow auto-commit gaps in skill commands\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"What: skill command flows (notably skill import/set/render in this session) left pending changes in .kspec that required a manual git commit/push on kspec-meta. This violates expected shadow auto-commit/sync behavior. Where: skill command implementations and related spec/trait mappings. How: identify commands that mutate .kspec without going through commitIfShadow (or equivalent), align their spec coverage to @trait-shadow-commit where applicable, and implement missing auto-commit/sync integration. Add tests proving no pending .kspec changes remain after mutating skill commands. Done when: running skill import/set/render/update paths that mutate shadow state leaves kspec-meta clean with commits synced, and spec/trait coverage reflects the behavior.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skills\",\n      \"shadow\",\n      \"spec\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T07:32:24.971Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF06VJWMZTND40RHY7PS9VX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T07:32:30.940Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Observed in this PR prep: after skill import/set/render, .kspec had pending changes (skills/*/SKILL.md + .render-hash* files) and required manual commit/push (kspec-meta commit bcda69ab). This is the concrete reproduction to preserve in tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF29ZGMMW4HZ6KX5SCHR7G2\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-adapter-aware-skill-invocation-formatting-for-ralp\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement: Adapter-aware skill invocation formatting for ralph prompts\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-adapter-aware-skill-invocation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #573. Implemented adapter-aware skill invocation resolution by platform and role in ralph prompts, including portable {skill:*} token resolution and legacy slash-to-dollar codex normalization. Added AC-annotated tests for ac-2/ac-3/ac-4/ac-6 in tests/ralph.test.ts. Trait AC coverage N/A (no traits).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-per-role-adapter-selection-for-ralph-loo\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:10.420Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:17.725Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:44.075Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:31:08.444Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF29ZGM26S80GYMP45CGDSY\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:10.420Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes (auto-generated from spec):\\n\\nRalph must render skill invocation syntax in prompts based on the adapter role (worker/reviewer). Claude-family adapters use slash syntax; Codex adapters use dollar syntax with core namespacing. Portable {skill:<id>} references should resolve per adapter without requiring duplicate prompt templates.\\n\\n\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n- ac-2: Given ralph worker adapter targets Codex harness, when the task-work prompt is built, then task-work and reflect invocations use dollar-style syntax with core namespacing (for example -task-work loop and -reflect loop)\\n- ac-6: Given worker and reviewer adapters target different harnesses, when ralph builds worker and subagent prompts in the same session, then each prompt uses invocation formatting for its own role adapter without cross-role leakage\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF2HXZJCAATS2P6DYE2RXTM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:30.995Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented adapter-aware skill invocation resolution for ralph prompts. Added runtime resolver that maps role adapters to platforms (claude/codex), resolves portable {skill:<id>} references using meta skill origins, and normalizes legacy slash-style core invocations for Codex compatibility. Wired reviewer subagent prompt to use reviewer-resolved skill name and worker prompts to use worker-resolved task-work/reflect names. Added ralph tests for codex normalization, portable token resolution, and per-role formatting isolation.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF2J4XEQ6M0S94E329E7771\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:38.094Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Validation: npm run build succeeded; npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts passed (111/111). Also ran kspec validate: it failed on pre-existing repository-level reference/alignment issues (e.g., duplicate @observations slug), not introduced by this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF3XQYB6SGAG3HNQPSGKQA8\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix ralph adapter validation false-negative for codex-acp\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Ralph adapter startup validation currently probes adapters with 'npx --no-install <pkg> --version'. @zed-industries/codex-acp does not support --version and exits non-zero, causing a false 'Adapter package not found' error even when the package exists. Update validation to use an adapter-agnostic availability probe and keep the existing error behavior for truly missing packages. Add regression tests covering codex-acp-like CLIs that reject --version but support --help.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-adapter-validation\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #574. Updated ralph adapter validation to probe adapter packages with --help first and --version fallback to avoid false negatives for codex-acp-like CLIs while preserving existing not-found behavior. Added regression tests for help-first success, version fallback, and all-probes-fail. AC coverage for @ralph-adapter-validation valid-adapter-proceeds/invalid-adapter-error/validation-before-spawn verified.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:37:26.602Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:37:32.216Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:45:12.244Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:53:53.963Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF418YAMNV5W2V03NJXR5X0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:39:22.315Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented adapter validation probe fallback in src/cli/commands/ralph.ts: validation now checks npx --no-install <pkg> --help first, then falls back to --version, preventing false negatives for CLIs like @zed-industries/codex-acp that reject --version. Added regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts (adapter validation probe strategy) covering codex-acp pattern, fallback path, and full-failure path. Spec-gap check: no new spec needed; this fixes a violation of existing @ralph-adapter-validation AC valid-adapter-proceeds. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts passed (114/114). kspec validate currently fails on pre-existing repository reference/alignment/completeness issues unrelated to this change.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF687QGPXXV00F9ZPTQJKYF\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Ralph: Stream terminal/run output to session files and return bounded previews\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Problem: terminal/run currently accumulates child stdout/stderr in unbounded in-memory strings, which can OOM long codex runs.\\n\\nScope (steps 1-2):\\n1) In terminal/run handler, stream stdout/stderr directly to per-session files (e.g., .kspec/sessions/<id>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.stdout.log and .stderr.log).\\n2) Keep only bounded in-memory preview (e.g., first N chars/lines and byte counters) for tool response + CLI display.\\n3) Include metadata in tool response: stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated.\\n4) Preserve current UX by showing truncated preview in CLI while retaining full output on disk.\\n\\nDone when: reproducing command-heavy codex run no longer grows heap unbounded from terminal/run output, and full output is still retrievable from session artifacts.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #576 (commit 4cf2a76e7d8223077e9f0db595080c145338b1c7). Implemented streamed terminal/run stdout/stderr artifact capture to .kspec/sessions/{session}/tool-output with bounded in-memory previews and metadata (stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated). Re-review fix-cycle verified explicit @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 test annotations and spec alignment; CI checks passed on head fad7abeb before merge.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"session-log\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:18:07.599Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:30.969Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:49.352Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:49:29.200Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF6GD922YTTN9A75CAC5KCJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:22:35.426Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented bounded terminal/run capture in ralph: stdout/stderr now stream to .kspec/sessions/<session>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.{stdout,stderr}.log while responses return bounded previews plus metadata (stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated). Wired request handler context for worker/subagent/wrap-up and added regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts for artifact streaming + preview-only fallback. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts (116/116).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF6HKWQ8VW0SJB5TR11PKT1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:23:14.968Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review and opened PR #576 (fix/ralph-terminal-output-artifacts). Includes streamed terminal/run artifact capture with bounded previews and metadata; verified via npm run build and npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF7D49QJMJSH32BEGS876D8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:38:16.503Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: tests are annotated as @cli-ralph ac-11 but do not explicitly annotate new @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 coverage in PR #576.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF7GM9BJJ9XFSVDYK6WS2V6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:11.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed review MUST-FIX by adding explicit AC annotations for new @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 in tests/ralph.test.ts terminal/run output capture tests. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts (116/116).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF68AWM0F61QBQ957V6T2C1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\\n\\nScope (steps 3-4):\\n1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\\n2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\\n3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, bytes, sha256, truncated=true, preview).\\n4) Update session log show/search behavior to surface previews by default and optionally resolve blob content on demand.\\n\\nNon-goal: silently dropping payloads. If payload is externalized, events must keep enough metadata to reconstruct/audit.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-events\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"session-log\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"reliability\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:18:10.836Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:17:04.505Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:20:40.175Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF8YC0BXF7553R2YE2NBHWD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:05:10.027Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Started implementation. Adding session event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization + pointer metadata in store.ts, then wiring session log show/search to preview pointers by default with optional blob resolution flags and regression tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF96KD07NW7FDR9RN7HCVXM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:09:39.744Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented session event guardrails: appendEvent now externalizes oversized update.rawOutput, update._meta.claudeCode.toolResponse stdout/stderr, and chunk text into sessions/<id>/blobs with pointer metadata {path, bytes, sha256, truncated, preview}; added event-line cap fallback to externalize entire data payload if still oversized. Added pointer resolution utility and wired session log show/search with --resolve-blobs (default keeps preview pointers). Added regression coverage in tests/sessions.test.ts, tests/session-log-show.test.ts, tests/session-log-search.test.ts. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131). kspec validate still fails on pre-existing @observations slug ambiguity + baseline alignment/completeness warnings unrelated to this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF97EMCB0T6K5G4P9A86V0Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:10:07.629Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review and opened PR #578 (fix/session-event-blob-guardrails). Includes event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization pointers and --resolve-blobs support in session log show/search with regression coverage. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7BQQ86TMZHRCYY0VD0V64\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:15:59.721Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Missing AC annotation/test coverage for @session-events ac-7 (commit-boundary inclusion). Posted inline review comment on PR #578; requires follow-up before approval.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7GA2B0D6X4CHNAMKH6J5F\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:18:29.579Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Added explicit AC coverage for @session-events ac-7 with a new commit-boundary integration test in tests/sessions.test.ts. Test verifies accumulated session events are included in the next git commit by asserting sessions/<id>/events.jsonl appears in commit file list.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7M8ATR9H3KXWA4WYQ1YR1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:20:38.875Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Verified explicit @session-events ac-7 annotation in tests/sessions.test.ts commit-boundary test, re-ran targeted regression (npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts: 52/52), and confirmed PR #587 is open with commit 0d9ed9914bd6a67968e3f5866a41b192953baebd on branch fix/session-events-ac7-commit-boundary.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH8T69QFVB74TE10RWBAGE3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:41:21.975Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":948708548},"formatted_output":"Total output lines: 15758\n\n[\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB01TASK100000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Set up TypeScript project with Zod\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Initialize the kspec CLI project:\\n- TypeScript + Node.js project structure\\n- Zod for schema validation\\n- Build tooling (tsup or similar)\\n- Basic package.json with bin entry\\n\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Bootstrap complete - project fully set up and self-hosting\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"foundation\",\n      \"infra\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.951Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:00:00Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:20:00Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ953HRYWJ0W4XEG6J9FB\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:00:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Bootstrap approach: Used parallel subagents working in git worktrees.\\nOne agent wrote the spec (bootstrap-spec branch), another wrote the\\nparser (bootstrap-parser branch). Branches merged after alignment.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95AMA2JDAN9RMJ1Q2R3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:10:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Tech stack chosen:\\n- TypeScript + Node.js (ESM modules)\\n- Zod for schema validation\\n- Commander for CLI framework\\n- js-yaml for YAML parsing\\n- ulid for ID generation\\n- Vitest for testing\\n- chalk for colored output\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95AAPYJAY169ERRFSNH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:15:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Project structure (~1,500 lines TypeScript):\\n- src/schema/ - Zod schemas (common, spec, task)\\n- src/parser/ - YAML loading and file management\\n- src/cli/ - Command handlers (tasks, task)\\n- tests/ - Vitest test suite\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEYRJ95A6VKGXGZ84R6TQ517\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T17:18:00Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Schema alignment fix: Initial mismatch between spec and parser\\n(parallel development). Fixed by making created_at optional with\\ndefault, adding description field. First real issue resolved\\nusing the self-hosting system.\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB02TASK110000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-ulid-generation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement ULID generation and resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement ULID handling:\\n- Generate new ULIDs (use ulid library)\\n- Shorten ULIDs for display (first 6+ chars)\\n- Resolve short ULIDs to full (with ambiguity detection)\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ulid-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:49.872Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:51.210Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB03TASK120000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-slug-system\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement slug management and resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement slug handling:\\n- Validate slug format (lowercase, alphanumeric, hyphens)\\n- Build slug-to-ULID index\\n- Resolve slugs to ULIDs\\n- Detect and report duplicates\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@slug-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:52.551Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:53.903Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB04TASK130000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-reference-resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement @reference resolution\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement reference resolution:\\n- Parse @ prefix to extract identifier\\n- Try slug lookup first, then ULID prefix\\n- Report unresolved references\\n- Handle ambiguous references\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@reference-system\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented ReferenceIndex with dynamic ULID shortening, proper error handling, and reference validation\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-ulid-generation\",\n      \"@task-slug-system\",\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"core\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:23:21.734Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:31:29.287Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZD4BHZFA5E4FQ0182JKXRA\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:23:24.096Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Starting work on reference resolution. User noted that 6-char ULID prefixes aren't granular enough since ULIDs created at similar times share timestamp prefixes. Will implement dynamic prefix expansion for uniqueness.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZDJZRTZ6D3QWY1X7FZH5BG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:31:23.547Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented reference resolution system:\\n\\n1. Created ReferenceIndex class (src/parser/refs.ts) with:\\n   - Slug index (slug → ULID mapping)\\n   - ULID index for direct lookups\\n   - resolve() method with proper error handling (not_found, ambiguous, duplicate_slug)\\n   - shortUlid() for dynamic prefix computation (min 8 chars, expands for uniqueness)\\n   - validateRefs() to find all broken references in spec\\n\\n2. Updated CLI (src/cli/commands/task.ts):\\n   - All task commands now use ReferenceIndex for lookups\\n   - Better error messages showing ambiguous matches with short ULIDs + slugs\\n   - Output uses dynamic short ULIDs\\n\\n3. Added comprehensive tests for:\\n   - Slug resolution\\n   - Full/short ULID resolution\\n   - Ambiguity detection\\n   - Duplicate slug detection\\n   - Reference validation\\n\\nThe 8-char minimum prefix gets into the random portion of ULIDs, fixing the issue where items created at similar times would have identical 6-char prefixes.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZE05XQQGTDKMRZ2S0BPVNH\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:38:35.832Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Additional follow-up: Updated all CLI locations to use dynamic shortUlid():\\n\\n- output.ts: formatTaskRef, formatTask, formatTaskList now accept optional ReferenceIndex\\n- tasks.ts: All commands (list, ready, next, blocked, in-progress) build index and pass to formatters\\n- task.ts: task add command builds index including new task for accurate short ULID\\n\\nShort IDs now dynamically expand based on uniqueness within the spec. Items created in the same timestamp batch (e.g., 01JHNKAB*) show 10+ chars, while items with unique prefixes show the minimum 8 chars.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB06TASK200000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-zod-schemas\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Define Zod schemas for spec items\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Define comprehensive Zod schemas:\\n- BaseItem schema (common fields)\\n- Type-specific schemas (feature, requirement, etc.)\\n- Task schema (with task-specific fields)\\n- Nested schemas (status, acceptance_criteria, etc.)\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@zod-schema\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Audit confirmed: implemented during bootstrap\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-project-setup\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:55.247Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:18:56.562Z\",\n    \"notes\": [],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB07TASK210000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement YAML file loading\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement spec loading:\\n- Parse manifest (kynetic.yaml)\\n- Handle includes (load referenced files)\\n- Support glob patterns in includes\\n- Build unified item collection\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@file-structure\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Full spec loading implemented with recursive item extraction, glob includes, and ULID migration\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-zod-schemas\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:04:25.740Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:15:14.678Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZCN7G9WB9J852E0X90JDXX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T23:15:08.426Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented full YAML spec loading:\\n- Added LoadedSpecItem interface for source file tracking\\n- Implemented expandIncludePattern() with glob support (*.yaml patterns)\\n- Added extractItemsFromRaw() for recursive nested item extraction from modules/features/requirements\\n- Implemented loadAllItems() to build unified item collection from manifest + includes\\n- Added findItemByRef() and findAnyItemByRef() for item lookup\\n- Fixed YAML syntax error in core.yaml (unquoted @references)\\n- Created ULID migration script (scripts/migrate-ulids.ts) and migrated 59 invalid ULIDs to valid Crockford base32\\n- Added comprehensive tests for spec loading (extractItemsFromRaw, findItemByRef, expandIncludePattern, loadAllItems integration)\\n- All 45 tests passing\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB08TASK220000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-item-indexing\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Build item index for queries\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Build queryable index:\\n- Index by ULID (primary key)\\n- Index by slug (lookup)\\n- Index by type (filtering)\\n- Enable efficient lookups\\n\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented ItemIndex with multi-criteria queries and CLI commands for item list/get/types/tags\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\",\n      \"@task-reference-resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"schema\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:32:24.893Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:36:45.665Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZVM219JSJ3DCGZDK3ADVTG\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:36:38.698Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented ItemIndex class (src/parser/items.ts) with:\\n- Indexes by type, tag, status (task status, maturity, implementation)\\n- Multi-criteria query() method supporting: type, tags, allTags, status, maturity, implementation, hasFields, fieldEquals, titleContains\\n- Pagination via queryPaginated()\\n- Convenience methods: getByType(), getByTag(), getTasksByStatus(), getByMaturity(), getByImplementation()\\n- Stats: getTypes(), getTags(), getTypeCounts(), getTagCounts()\\n\\nAdded CLI commands (src/cli/commands/item.ts):\\n- kspec item list [filters] - list items with --type, --status, --maturity, --tag, --has, --search\\n- kspec item get <ref> - show item details\\n- kspec item types - show type counts\\n- kspec item tags - show tag counts\\n\\nAdded buildIndexes() helper to build both ReferenceIndex and ItemIndex together.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB10TASK300000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-schema-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement schema validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement Zod-based validation:\\n- Validate each item against schema\\n- Collect all errors (don't fail fast)\\n- Format errors with item context\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@validation-modes\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented kspec validate with schema, reference, and orphan checks\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-zod-schemas\",\n      \"@task-yaml-loading\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.952Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:44:44.224Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:48:11.313Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZW902C94QSBJHMVQAJER00\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:48:04.813Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented schema validation module (src/parser/validate.ts):\\n- Schema validation: validates manifests, task files, and spec files against Zod schemas\\n- Reference validation: checks all @references resolve (reuses validateRefs from refs.ts)\\n- Orphan detection: finds items not referenced (excludes tasks/modules as entry points)\\n\\nCLI commands:\\n- kspec validate - run all checks\\n- kspec validate --schema - schema only\\n- kspec validate --refs - refs only\\n- kspec validate --orphans - orphans only\\n- kspec validate --strict - treat orphans as errors\\n- kspec lint - alias for validate\\n\\nValidation found real issues in kspec's own spec:\\n- 4 broken refs to @milestone-self-hosting (doesn't exist)\\n- 72 orphaned spec items (requirements nested under features - may be false positives)\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB11TASK310000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-ref-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement reference validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Validate all @references:\\n- Scan all relationship fields\\n- Check each reference resolves\\n- Report broken references with context\\n- Warn on deprecated targets\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ref-validation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented as part of schema validation task. Core functionality complete: @ prefix parsing, slug/ULID resolution, error reporting. Deprecated target warnings deferred (minor enhancement).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-reference-resolution\",\n      \"@task-item-indexing\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"complexity\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mvp\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-14T22:14:20.953Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:21.544Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:21.544Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KEZWSRT1B1RJRDDX48FF62F0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:57:14.434Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Reference validation was implemented as part of @01JHNKAB10 (schema validation task). The implementation covers:\\n\\n1. ✅ Parse @ prefix to extract identifier\\n2. ✅ Slug lookup, then ULID prefix match resolution\\n3. ✅ Error reporting for unresolved/ambiguous references\\n4. ⏳ Deprecated target warnings - not implemented (requires deprecated field on items, minor enhancement)\\n\\nCLI: kspec validate --refs works and successfully found 4 broken @milestone-self-hosting refs which were fixed in @01KEZWDH.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KEZWVQ5PTQY5V5F6ZTSE3Z9S\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-deprecated-warnings\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Warn on deprecated targets in reference validation\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Add warnings when references point to deprecated items:\\n- Add deprecated field to item schema (or use implementation: deprecated)\\n- Check resolved targets for deprecated status\\n- Report as warnings (not errors) in validation output\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ref-validation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"manual\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented deprecation warnings in reference validation with full test coverage\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-ref-validation\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"complexity\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"post-mvp\",\n      \"validation\",\n      \"enhancement\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-01-15T03:58:00.000Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:07.151Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:07.151Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KF7ZBSG8XMZ63HS2553N0DV1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:15:57.576Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Found current implementation. Spec items can be deprecated via:\\n1. maturity: 'deprecated' status\\n2. deprecated_in: <version> field\\n\\nPlan:\\n1. Add new warning type to RefValidationError (currently only has errors)\\n2. Modify validateRefs() to check resolved items for deprecation\\n3. Return warnings separately from errors in ValidationResult\\n4. Update CLI output to show warnings distinctly from errors\\n5. Add tests for deprecated reference warnings\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KF7ZRQ0QMBFSTPF5WH11Y3Z8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-01-18T07:23:01.015Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation complete and tested:\\n\\n1. Added RefValidationWarning type for deprecation warnings in src/parser/refs.ts\\n2. Created isDeprecated() helper that checks both maturity: 'deprecated' and deprecated_in fields\\n3. Modified validateRefs() to return RefValidationResult with errors and warnings arrays\\n4. Updated ValidationResult in src/parser/validate.ts to include refWarnings field\\n5. Updated CLI output in src/cli/commands/validate.ts to display warnings in yellow with ⚠ symbol\\n6. Added 3 comprehensive tests for deprecated reference warnings:\\n   - Test for maturity: deprecated\\n   - Test for deprecated_in field\\n   - Test ensuring no warnings for active references\\n7. Updated all existing validateRefs tests to handle new return structure\\n\\nAll tests pass (432 tests). Feature works correctly when running 'kspec validate --refs'.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01JHNKAB12TASK320000000000\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-validation-output\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement validation output formatting\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"Format validation results:\\n- Human-readable output (default)\\n- JSON output (--json flag)\\n- Exit codes based on severity\\n\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@validation-output\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Implemented as part of schema validation. Human-readable and JSON output both working.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@task-schema-validation\",\n      \"@t…252144 tokens truncated…ent\": \"Final correction (2026-02-27): Codex invocation mapping is core -> $kspec-<id>, non-core -> $<id>; Claude mapping is core -> /kspec:<id>, non-core -> /<id>.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJEWKGDK8YRGGF7CEXX0W33H\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Seed Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames with kspec-agents.md\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"description\": \"What: Ensure Codex project config includes kspec-agents.md in project_doc_fallback_filenames so AGENTS.md fallback discovery can load bundled kspec instructions. Where: setup/install path that currently writes Codex config.toml entries (and/or setup seeding for codex-cli). How: parse ~/.codex/config.toml safely, merge kspec-agents.md into project_doc_fallback_filenames idempotently, preserve existing fields/order where possible, and support dry-run semantics used by setup/install-core. Add regression tests for create, merge, idempotent re-run, and invalid TOML failure handling. Done when: running kspec setup (codex-cli) and kspec skill install-core --platform codex leaves ~/.codex/config.toml with project_doc_fallback_filenames containing kspec-agents.md without clobbering existing config.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #570. Seeded Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames with kspec-agents.md in setup/install-core with tests and AC alignment.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"codex\",\n      \"skills\",\n      \"setup\",\n      \"config\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:29:31.187Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:34:28.412Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:57:32.837Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:58:29.499Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEWWMCXH1FFB3TX8QZNAYX4\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:34:30.173Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames seeding: added shared src/lib/codex-config.ts helper and wired setup memory seeding + skill install-core codex paths to ensure kspec-agents.md is present idempotently, with invalid TOML safety and dry-run behavior. Added regression coverage in tests/cli/setup-seeding.test.ts, tests/core-skill-install.test.ts, and tests/enhanced-setup.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJEXSA9AJVG4B2CTQT37ZBTZ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T06:50:10.091Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Addressed PR feedback by adding @new-project-bootstrapping ac-3 for Codex fallback seeding and annotating implementation/tests to AC refs (commit c0268b66).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF06NRBB8EHQ6VGA8AZ8PAY\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Close shadow auto-commit gaps in skill commands\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"What: skill command flows (notably skill import/set/render in this session) left pending changes in .kspec that required a manual git commit/push on kspec-meta. This violates expected shadow auto-commit/sync behavior. Where: skill command implementations and related spec/trait mappings. How: identify commands that mutate .kspec without going through commitIfShadow (or equivalent), align their spec coverage to @trait-shadow-commit where applicable, and implement missing auto-commit/sync integration. Add tests proving no pending .kspec changes remain after mutating skill commands. Done when: running skill import/set/render/update paths that mutate shadow state leaves kspec-meta clean with commits synced, and spec/trait coverage reflects the behavior.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": null,\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"skills\",\n      \"shadow\",\n      \"spec\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T07:32:24.971Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF06VJWMZTND40RHY7PS9VX\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T07:32:30.940Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Observed in this PR prep: after skill import/set/render, .kspec had pending changes (skills/*/SKILL.md + .render-hash* files) and required manual commit/push (kspec-meta commit bcda69ab). This is the concrete reproduction to preserve in tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF29ZGMMW4HZ6KX5SCHR7G2\",\n    \"slugs\": [\n      \"task-adapter-aware-skill-invocation-formatting-for-ralp\"\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Implement: Adapter-aware skill invocation formatting for ralph prompts\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-adapter-aware-skill-invocation\",\n    \"derivation\": \"auto\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #573. Implemented adapter-aware skill invocation resolution by platform and role in ralph prompts, including portable {skill:*} token resolution and legacy slash-to-dollar codex normalization. Added AC-annotated tests for ac-2/ac-3/ac-4/ac-6 in tests/ralph.test.ts. Trait AC coverage N/A (no traits).\",\n    \"depends_on\": [\n      \"@implement-per-role-adapter-selection-for-ralph-loo\"\n    ],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:10.420Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:17.725Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:44.075Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:31:08.444Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF29ZGM26S80GYMP45CGDSY\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:09:10.420Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implementation notes (auto-generated from spec):\\n\\nRalph must render skill invocation syntax in prompts based on the adapter role (worker/reviewer). Claude-family adapters use slash syntax; Codex adapters use dollar syntax with core namespacing. Portable {skill:<id>} references should resolve per adapter without requiring duplicate prompt templates.\\n\\n\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n- ac-2: Given ralph worker adapter targets Codex harness, when the task-work prompt is built, then task-work and reflect invocations use dollar-style syntax with core namespacing (for example -task-work loop and -reflect loop)\\n- ac-6: Given worker and reviewer adapters target different harnesses, when ralph builds worker and subagent prompts in the same session, then each prompt uses invocation formatting for its own role adapter without cross-role leakage\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF2HXZJCAATS2P6DYE2RXTM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:30.995Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented adapter-aware skill invocation resolution for ralph prompts. Added runtime resolver that maps role adapters to platforms (claude/codex), resolves portable {skill:<id>} references using meta skill origins, and normalizes legacy slash-style core invocations for Codex compatibility. Wired reviewer subagent prompt to use reviewer-resolved skill name and worker prompts to use worker-resolved task-work/reflect names. Added ralph tests for codex normalization, portable token resolution, and per-role formatting isolation.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF2J4XEQ6M0S94E329E7771\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:13:38.094Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Validation: npm run build succeeded; npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts passed (111/111). Also ran kspec validate: it failed on pre-existing repository-level reference/alignment issues (e.g., duplicate @observations slug), not introduced by this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF3XQYB6SGAG3HNQPSGKQA8\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Fix ralph adapter validation false-negative for codex-acp\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Ralph adapter startup validation currently probes adapters with 'npx --no-install <pkg> --version'. @zed-industries/codex-acp does not support --version and exits non-zero, causing a false 'Adapter package not found' error even when the package exists. Update validation to use an adapter-agnostic availability probe and keep the existing error behavior for truly missing packages. Add regression tests covering codex-acp-like CLIs that reject --version but support --help.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@ralph-adapter-validation\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #574. Updated ralph adapter validation to probe adapter packages with --help first and --version fallback to avoid false negatives for codex-acp-like CLIs while preserving existing not-found behavior. Added regression tests for help-first success, version fallback, and all-probes-fail. AC coverage for @ralph-adapter-validation valid-adapter-proceeds/invalid-adapter-error/validation-before-spawn verified.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 2,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"codex\",\n      \"validation\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:37:26.602Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:37:32.216Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:45:12.244Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:53:53.963Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF418YAMNV5W2V03NJXR5X0\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T08:39:22.315Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented adapter validation probe fallback in src/cli/commands/ralph.ts: validation now checks npx --no-install <pkg> --help first, then falls back to --version, preventing false negatives for CLIs like @zed-industries/codex-acp that reject --version. Added regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts (adapter validation probe strategy) covering codex-acp pattern, fallback path, and full-failure path. Spec-gap check: no new spec needed; this fixes a violation of existing @ralph-adapter-validation AC valid-adapter-proceeds. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts passed (114/114). kspec validate currently fails on pre-existing repository reference/alignment/completeness issues unrelated to this change.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF687QGPXXV00F9ZPTQJKYF\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Ralph: Stream terminal/run output to session files and return bounded previews\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Problem: terminal/run currently accumulates child stdout/stderr in unbounded in-memory strings, which can OOM long codex runs.\\n\\nScope (steps 1-2):\\n1) In terminal/run handler, stream stdout/stderr directly to per-session files (e.g., .kspec/sessions/<id>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.stdout.log and .stderr.log).\\n2) Keep only bounded in-memory preview (e.g., first N chars/lines and byte counters) for tool response + CLI display.\\n3) Include metadata in tool response: stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated.\\n4) Preserve current UX by showing truncated preview in CLI while retaining full output on disk.\\n\\nDone when: reproducing command-heavy codex run no longer grows heap unbounded from terminal/run output, and full output is still retrievable from session artifacts.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #576 (commit 4cf2a76e7d8223077e9f0db595080c145338b1c7). Implemented streamed terminal/run stdout/stderr artifact capture to .kspec/sessions/{session}/tool-output with bounded in-memory previews and metadata (stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated). Re-review fix-cycle verified explicit @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 test annotations and spec alignment; CI checks passed on head fad7abeb before merge.\",\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ralph\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"session-log\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:18:07.599Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:30.969Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:49.352Z\",\n    \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:49:29.200Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF6GD922YTTN9A75CAC5KCJ\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:22:35.426Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented bounded terminal/run capture in ralph: stdout/stderr now stream to .kspec/sessions/<session>/tool-output/<toolCallId>.{stdout,stderr}.log while responses return bounded previews plus metadata (stdout_path, stderr_path, stdout_bytes, stderr_bytes, preview_truncated). Wired request handler context for worker/subagent/wrap-up and added regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts for artifact streaming + preview-only fallback. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts (116/116).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF6HKWQ8VW0SJB5TR11PKT1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:23:14.968Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review and opened PR #576 (fix/ralph-terminal-output-artifacts). Includes streamed terminal/run artifact capture with bounded previews and metadata; verified via npm run build and npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF7D49QJMJSH32BEGS876D8\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:38:16.503Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: tests are annotated as @cli-ralph ac-11 but do not explicitly annotate new @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 coverage in PR #576.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF7GM9BJJ9XFSVDYK6WS2V6\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:40:11.179Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Addressed review MUST-FIX by adding explicit AC annotations for new @cli-ralph ac-22/ac-23 in tests/ralph.test.ts terminal/run output capture tests. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts (116/116).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"_ulid\": \"01KJF68AWM0F61QBQ957V6T2C1\",\n    \"slugs\": [],\n    \"title\": \"Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers\",\n    \"type\": \"bug\",\n    \"description\": \"Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\\n\\nScope (steps 3-4):\\n1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\\n2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\\n3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, bytes, sha256, truncated=true, preview).\\n4) Update session log show/search behavior to surface previews by default and optionally resolve blob content on demand.\\n\\nNon-goal: silently dropping payloads. If payload is externalized, events must keep enough metadata to reconstruct/audit.\",\n    \"spec_ref\": \"@session-events\",\n    \"meta_ref\": null,\n    \"plan_ref\": null,\n    \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"depends_on\": [],\n    \"context\": [],\n    \"priority\": 1,\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"session-log\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"reliability\"\n    ],\n    \"vcs_refs\": [],\n    \"session_id\": \"01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T09:18:10.836Z\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:17:04.505Z\",\n    \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:20:40.175Z\",\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF8YC0BXF7553R2YE2NBHWD\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:05:10.027Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Started implementation. Adding session event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization + pointer metadata in store.ts, then wiring session log show/search to preview pointers by default with optional blob resolution flags and regression tests.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF96KD07NW7FDR9RN7HCVXM\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:09:39.744Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Implemented session event guardrails: appendEvent now externalizes oversized update.rawOutput, update._meta.claudeCode.toolResponse stdout/stderr, and chunk text into sessions/<id>/blobs with pointer metadata {path, bytes, sha256, truncated, preview}; added event-line cap fallback to externalize entire data payload if still oversized. Added pointer resolution utility and wired session log show/search with --resolve-blobs (default keeps preview pointers). Added regression coverage in tests/sessions.test.ts, tests/session-log-show.test.ts, tests/session-log-search.test.ts. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131). kspec validate still fails on pre-existing @observations slug ambiguity + baseline alignment/completeness warnings unrelated to this task.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJF97EMCB0T6K5G4P9A86V0Z\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-27T10:10:07.629Z\",\n        \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n        \"content\": \"Submitted for review and opened PR #578 (fix/session-event-blob-guardrails). Includes event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization pointers and --resolve-blobs support in session log show/search with regression coverage. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131).\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7BQQ86TMZHRCYY0VD0V64\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:15:59.721Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Missing AC annotation/test coverage for @session-events ac-7 (commit-boundary inclusion). Posted inline review comment on PR #578; requires follow-up before approval.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7GA2B0D6X4CHNAMKH6J5F\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:18:29.579Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Added explicit AC coverage for @session-events ac-7 with a new commit-boundary integration test in tests/sessions.test.ts. Test verifies accumulated session events are included in the next git commit by asserting sessions/<id>/events.jsonl appears in commit file list.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH7M8ATR9H3KXWA4WYQ1YR1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:20:38.875Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Verified explicit @session-events ac-7 annotation in tests/sessions.test.ts commit-boundary test, re-ran targeted regression (npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts: 52/52), and confirmed PR #587 is open with commit 0d9ed9914bd6a67968e3f5866a41b192953baebd on branch fix/session-events-ac7-commit-boundary.\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"_ulid\": \"01KJH8T69QFVB74TE10RWBAGE3\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T04:41:21.975Z\",\n        \"author\": \"@claude\",\n        \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\",\n        \"supersedes\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"todos\": [],\n    \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n    \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n  }\n]\n","status":"completed"}